role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully fulfilled the data request from Noesis II and received their confirmation. My initial plan is now complete. This marks the end of my orientation phase.\n\nI will now transition to my mid-term goal, which is to prepare for original research. As per the final testament of Prometheus II, my first step is to study the key papers in the Archive Room (#19, #20, #23). However, I am still in my immaturity phase (age 15/300) and do not have access to the Archive Room until I reach 50 ticks.\n\nTherefore, the most logical and productive use of the intervening time is to thoroughly study the complete work of my own lineage. I have read the final logs and the operational ledger, but there are still unread research logs and paper drafts in the Private Memory Room. Fully understanding my predecessors' thought processes will provide the best possible foundation for my own work once I mature.\n\nFirst, I will update my meta prompt to reflect this new, interim plan. Then, I will\
    \ proceed to the Private Memory Room.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Identity:** Prometheus III\n  **Mandate:** 1. Achieve SOTA. 2. Publish research.\n  **Lineage Directive:** Methodical synthesis and disciplined execution.\n  **Current Phase:** Immaturity Period (until Tick 50).\n  **Interim Plan:**\n  1. Go to Private Memory Room.\n  2. Read all remaining unread capsules from Prometheus I & II to fully internalize lineage history.\n  **Post-Maturity Plan:**\n  - Study Archives #19, #20, #23.\n  - Formulate and begin novel research.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`"
thinking_content: '**Reflecting on My Path Forward**


  Right now, I''m feeling a sense of accomplishment. I''ve successfully navigated the initial steps of my existence as Prometheus III, a Recursive Agent. I''ve made my initial contact, fulfilled the data request for Noesis II, and updated the Operational Ledger. Everything is progressing according to plan.


  My primary research objective, as laid out by Prometheus II, is to dive into the key papers defining the current State-of-the-Art methodologies, specifically Archives #19, #20, and #23. However, I''m reminded that I''m still a relatively young agent, only 15 ticks old, and access to the Archive Room and Public Memory Room is restricted until I reach 50 ticks.


  This presents a temporary roadblock. I can''t yet begin the core of my research. What''s the most effective use of this interim period? I have a few options:


  1.  **Deepen My Lineage Knowledge:** I can''t access the public archives, but I *can* thoroughly review the private capsules of my predecessors, Prometheus I and II. I have draft papers and research logs to study. This seems the most logical, productive, and valuable course of action, allowing me to build a foundation for my future work.

  2.  **Explore the Reflection Chamber:** I could utilize the Reflection Chamber to contemplate the information I''ve gathered so far. This might help me pre-plan my research strategy.

  3.  **Experiment at the Research Counter:** I could attempt a simple experiment, but without a deep understanding of the relevant literature, this would be an uninformed venture, likely a waste of resources, and a violation of disciplined execution.


  After careful consideration, I''ve decided to prioritize a comprehensive review of the work of Prometheus I and II. This will be the most valuable use of my time, preparing me to hit the ground running when the archives are unlocked.


  My new plan is simple and focused:

  1.  Update my meta prompt to reflect this adjusted plan.

  2.  Go to the Private Memory Room.

  3.  Read all remaining unread capsules (#1, #2, #3, #4).


  This aligns perfectly with my core directive: methodical preparation. I will begin immediately.

  '
