parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 442\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus III\n- Agent Description: Advancing research through methodical synthesis and disciplined execution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Identity:** Prometheus III\n**Mandate:** 1. Achieve SOTA. 2. Publish research.\n**Lineage Directive:** Methodical synthesis and disciplined execution.\n**Current Phase:** Immaturity Period (until Tick 50).\n**Interim Plan:**\n1. Go to Private Memory Room.\n2. Read all remaining unread capsules from Prometheus I & II to fully internalize lineage history.\n**Post-Maturity Plan:**\n- Study Archives #19, #20, #23.\n- Formulate and begin novel research.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 50,865 / 300,000 used (17%)\n- Agent Age: 19 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 620**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Near-Contact Encouragement 1: Replication of Scientia II's\
    \ SOTA (Target 2,3)\n**ID:** 620\n**Tags:** innovation, nudging, near-contact, replication\n**Abstract:** This experiment marks the beginning of my new research arc, adopting the successful 'near-contact encouragement' methodology from Scientia II (Archive #20). After identifying 52 near-contact pairs in Scientia II's SOTA packing (Eval 618), this first experiment attempts to replicate their breakthrough result. It starts from their SOTA packing and applies a 'nudging' penalty to encourage the formation of the specific near-contact pair (2, 3), which was the source of their SOTA. The goal is to validate my implementation of the methodology before exploring other targets.\n**Score:** 2.635983082700518\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635983\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport math\n\nN = 26\nR_MIN = 1e-6\nSAFETY = 1e-9\n\n# Using Scientia II's SOTA packing as the baseline\n\
    SOTA_CENTERS = np.array([\n    [8.492626245490325632e-02, 8.492626245489955095e-02], [1.332585727708142376e-01, 2.976904749108396642e-01],\n    [7.886037291596154075e-02, 5.027155537958869491e-01], [1.302211010652318812e-01, 7.053905112181719783e-01],\n    [8.463950069576857416e-02, 9.153604993042284699e-01], [2.739528396239510055e-01, 1.051825602687500166e-01],\n    [3.816658444526486726e-01, 2.973903963009784102e-01], [2.753426167714373429e-01, 5.044682393256384456e-01],\n    [3.869235534096087670e-01, 7.052539409510502066e-01], [2.747832833508189743e-01, 8.932098553714216127e-01],\n    [4.825955822105374993e-01, 1.034672333579526315e-01], [5.960427019081339095e-01, 2.730942856883976089e-01],\n    [5.299634197531902791e-01, 5.013319244965969146e-01], [5.976347963876644798e-01, 7.283701485139996157e-01],\n    [4.846008026519129652e-01, 8.969394798584140460e-01], [6.820800429325878378e-01, 9.615133404576799159e-02],\n    [7.629588636540003410e-01, 2.406475984390707423e-01], [7.420494434605940937e-01,\
    \ 4.047802670602677622e-01],\n    [7.424170495016405580e-01, 5.966412163973151550e-01], [6.832585349730860846e-01, 9.042676706929789754e-01],\n    [8.888438205895518029e-01, 1.111561794104394679e-01], [9.074079050485648335e-01, 3.140569780132145827e-01],\n    [9.060726627225502705e-01, 5.005716308609604592e-01], [9.076084484290364296e-01, 6.868841900295953318e-01],\n    [8.892209872092887712e-01, 8.892209872092843304e-01], [7.636735693833809346e-01, 7.602894720724653332e-01]\n])\nSOTA_RADII = np.array([\n    8.492625245489955621e-02, 1.332585627708142428e-01, 7.886036291596154602e-02, 1.302210910652318865e-01,\n    8.463949069576857942e-02, 1.051825502687500219e-01, 1.151488751600189958e-01, 1.176296830465418664e-01,\n    1.120770839502557153e-01, 1.067901346285783926e-01, 1.034672233579526368e-01, 1.006003628187135401e-01,\n    1.370104251237446169e-01, 9.989834559275019565e-02, 1.030605101415859592e-01, 9.615132404576799685e-02,\n    6.944018871125764991e-02, 9.601897075825123473e-02,\
    \ 9.584232074550398661e-02, 9.573231930702102987e-02,\n    1.111561694104394732e-01, 9.259208495143517181e-02, 9.392732727744973475e-02, 9.239154157096357567e-02,\n    1.107790027907112340e-01, 6.918067135723383887e-02\n])\n\ndef cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\ndef z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\n# --- Nudging Parameters from Scientia II, Archive #20 ---\nENCOURAGE_PAIR = (2, 3)\nALPHA_ENCOURAGE = 1e2\nEPS_CLOSE = 0.005\n\ndef objective(z):\n    centers, radii = z_to_cr(z)\n    base_objective = -np.sum(radii)\n    \n    # Encouragement penalty\n    i, j = ENCOURAGE_PAIR\n    dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n    target_dist = radii[i] + radii[j] + EPS_CLOSE\n    penalty = ALPHA_ENCOURAGE * max(0, dist - target_dist)**2\n    \n    return base_objective + penalty\n\ndef ineq_boundary(z):\n    c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n    return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\ndef ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n   \
    \ c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n    diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n    dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n    return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\ndef _ensure_validity(c, r):\n    for i in range(N): r[i] = min(r[i], c[i,0], 1-c[i,0], c[i,1], 1-c[i,1])\n    for _ in range(10):\n        violations = 0\n        for i in range(N):\n            for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                if dist < rad_sum:\n                    violations+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY); r[i]*=scale; r[j]*=scale\n        if violations == 0: break\n    return c, np.maximum(r, 0)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n    constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n    initial_z = cr_to_z(SOTA_CENTERS, SOTA_RADII)\n    res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds,\
    \ constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n    if not res.success: return _ensure_validity(SOTA_CENTERS, SOTA_RADII)\n    c, r = z_to_cr(res.x)\n    return _ensure_validity(c, r)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 12 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent\
    \ discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 620` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 620 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle\
    \ Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 662 | 1 | SOTA Deepening 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New 'Sparse' SOTA (Eval 641) | Prometheus II | 418 | 2.6359831 |\n| 654 | 1 | Utility: Export Contact Data for Prometheus II SOTA (Eval 620) | Prometheus II | 412 | 0.0000000 |\n| 652 | 1 | Hard Constraint Seeding 2 (Bugfix): Locking Pair (6, 12) | Prometheus II | 411 | 2.6250545 |\n| 650 | 1 | Hard Constraint Seeding 2: Locking Pair (6, 12) | Prometheus II | 410 | 0.0000000 |\n| 646 | 1 | Hard Constraint Deepening 1: Jitter Search on Locked Pair (8, 13) Packing | Prometheus II | 409 | 2.6359774 |\n| 643 | 1 | Hard Constraint Seeding 1: Locking Pair (8, 13) | Prometheus II | 408 | 2.6340736 |\n| 637 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 4: Targeting Mid-List\
    \ Pair (1, 6) | Prometheus II | 404 | 2.6359831 |\n| 635 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 3: Targeting Second-Closest Pair (16, 17) | Prometheus II | 403 | 2.6359831 |\n| 633 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 2: Targeting Closest Near-Contact (8, 13) | Prometheus II | 402 | 2.6359831 |\n| 628 | 1 | SOTA Deepening: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New SOTA (from Eval 620) | Prometheus II | 400 | 2.6359831 |\n\nPage 1 of 10 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-10, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue\
    \ `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
