tick: 448
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am in the Research Counter. My planning phase is complete, and now I begin execution.\n\nMy immediate goal is to develop the core components of my JAX-accelerated Genetic Algorithm. A modular approach is best. I will write the helper functions and the main GA class to a file in my lineage's storage. This allows me to build the logic incrementally and reuse it in future experiments without resubmitting the entire codebase each time. This is an efficient use of tokens and good scientific practice.\n\nI will start by creating a file named `ga_core.py` and writing the initial GA framework, including the JAX-based fitness function.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write prometheus/ga_core.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n\n  class JaxGA:\n      def __init__(self, key, population_size, chromosome_length, mutation_rate, crossover_rate):\n          self.key = key\n          self.population_size = population_size\n          self.chromosome_length\
    \ = chromosome_length\n          self.mutation_rate = mutation_rate\n          self.crossover_rate = crossover_rate\n          self.n_circles = 26\n\n      def init_population(self, initial_packings):\n          # initial_packings should be a list/array of (centers, radii) tuples\n          # This function will convert them into a flat chromosome representation\n          population = []\n          for centers, radii in initial_packings:\n              chromosome = jnp.concatenate([centers.flatten(), radii])\n              population.append(chromosome)\n          return jnp.array(population)\n\n      @staticmethod\n      @jax.jit\n      def _decode_chromosome(chromosome):\n          centers = chromosome[:2*26].reshape((26, 2))\n          radii = chromosome[2*26:]\n          return centers, radii\n\n      @staticmethod\n      @jax.jit\n      def calculate_fitness(chromosome):\n          centers, radii = JaxGA._decode_chromosome(chromosome)\n          \n          # Objective: maximize\
    \ sum of radii\n          objective = jnp.sum(radii)\n\n          # Penalty for radii <= 0\n          radii_penalty = jnp.sum(jax.nn.relu(-radii + 1e-7)) * 1e6\n\n          # Penalty for being outside the unit square\n          bounds_penalty_x = jnp.sum(jax.nn.relu(centers[:, 0] + radii - 1)) + jnp.sum(jax.nn.relu(-centers[:, 0] + radii))\n          bounds_penalty_y = jnp.sum(jax.nn.relu(centers[:, 1] + radii - 1)) + jnp.sum(jax.nn.relu(-centers[:, 1] + radii))\n          bounds_penalty = (bounds_penalty_x + bounds_penalty_y) * 1e6\n\n          # Penalty for overlaps\n          dist_matrix = jnp.sqrt(jnp.sum((centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1))\n          radii_sum_matrix = radii[:, None] + radii[None, :]\n          \n          # Get upper triangle, excluding diagonal\n          iu = jnp.triu_indices(26, 1)\n          overlaps = jax.nn.relu(radii_sum_matrix[iu] - dist_matrix[iu])\n          overlap_penalty = jnp.sum(overlaps) * 1e6\n          \n          total_penalty\
    \ = radii_penalty + bounds_penalty + overlap_penalty\n          return objective - total_penalty\n      \n      # Other methods (selection, crossover, mutation) will be added here\n      # ...\n```"
