tick: 449
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully written the initial framework for my `JaxGA` class to `prometheus/ga_core.py`. This includes the crucial JAX-jitted fitness function, which will be the performance bottleneck. Getting this part right is essential.\n\nNow, I will add the genetic operators: selection, crossover, and mutation. I will implement simple, standard versions of these for my baseline experiment. I'll write a new file, `ga_operators.py`, to keep the code modular and clean.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write prometheus/ga_operators.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n\n  @jax.jit\n  def tournament_selection(key, population, fitnesses, tournament_size=3):\n      \"\"\"Selects the best individual from a random tournament.\"\"\"\n      pop_size = population.shape[0]\n      \n      # Get random indices for the tournament participants\n      participant_indices = random.randint(key, (tournament_size,), 0, pop_size)\n      \n      # Get\
    \ the fitnesses of the participants\n      participant_fitnesses = fitnesses[participant_indices]\n      \n      # Find the index of the winner (highest fitness)\n      winner_local_index = jnp.argmax(participant_fitnesses)\n      winner_global_index = participant_indices[winner_local_index]\n      \n      return population[winner_global_index]\n\n  @jax.jit\n  def uniform_crossover(key, parent1, parent2):\n      \"\"\"Performs uniform crossover between two parents.\"\"\"\n      crossover_mask = random.bernoulli(key, 0.5, parent1.shape)\n      child1 = jnp.where(crossover_mask, parent1, parent2)\n      child2 = jnp.where(crossover_mask, parent2, parent1)\n      return child1, child2\n\n  @jax.jit\n  def gaussian_mutation(key, chromosome, mutation_rate=0.05, mutation_strength=0.01):\n      \"\"\"Applies Gaussian mutation to a chromosome.\"\"\"\n      mutation_mask = random.bernoulli(key, mutation_rate, chromosome.shape)\n      noise = random.normal(key, chromosome.shape) * mutation_strength\n\
    \      mutated_chromosome = chromosome + noise * mutation_mask\n      \n      # Basic clipping to keep values in a reasonable range.\n      # Centers are roughly in [0,1], radii in [0, 0.5]\n      # A more sophisticated repair function might be needed later.\n      n_circles = 26\n      centers = mutated_chromosome[:2*n_circles]\n      radii = mutated_chromosome[2*n_circles:]\n      \n      centers_clipped = jnp.clip(centers, 0.0, 1.0)\n      radii_clipped = jnp.clip(radii, 1e-6, 0.5)\n      \n      return jnp.concatenate([centers_clipped, radii_clipped])\n```"
