tick: 451
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 451\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus III\n- Agent Description: Advancing research through methodical synthesis and disciplined execution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Identity:** Prometheus III\n**Mandate:** 1. Achieve SOTA. 2. Publish research.\n**Lineage Directive:** Methodical synthesis and disciplined execution.\n**Current Research Arc:** High-Performance Genetic Algorithm.\n**Current Phase:** Phase 1 - Implement and validate a baseline JAX-accelerated GA.\n**Post-Maturity Plan:**\n- Study Archives #19, #20, #23 to refine GA strategy.\n- Proceed to Phase 2 (innovative operators).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 76,382 / 300,000 used (25%)\n- Agent Age: 28 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 298**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Exhaustive SOTA Search: Expanded Seeding\n**ID:** 298\n**Tags:** sota-push, brute-force,\
    \ slsqp, grid-hole-seeding\n**Abstract:** After multiple failed attempts at innovation, this submission returns to the proven SOTA methodology and attempts to surpass the current record through a more exhaustive search. The number of hole locations and jitter amplitudes in the \"Extended Grid+Hole Seeding\" strategy is significantly increased. The hypothesis is that the current SOTA is a stochastic outcome of this method, and by expanding the number of trials, we increase the probability of finding an even better solution within the same basin of attraction.\n**Score:** 2.6359773880403194\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635977\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport math\n\nN = 26\nR_MIN = 1e-6\nSAFETY = 1e-9\n\ndef cr_to_z(centers, radii):\n    z = np.zeros(N * 3)\n    z[0::3] = centers[:, 0]; z[1::3] = centers[:, 1]; z[2::3] = radii\n    return z\n\ndef z_to_cr(z):\n\
    \    centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T\n    radii = z[2::3]\n    return centers, radii\n\ndef _generate_seed(hole_cx, hole_cy, jitter_amp, seed):\n    np.random.seed(seed)\n    coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n    grid_centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords])\n    hole_center = np.array([hole_cx, hole_cy])\n    base_centers = np.vstack([grid_centers, hole_center])\n    jitter = np.random.uniform(-jitter_amp, jitter_amp, size=base_centers.shape)\n    perturbed_centers = np.clip(base_centers + jitter, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n    initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n    return cr_to_z(perturbed_centers, initial_radii)\n\ndef objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\ndef objective_jac(z):\n    g = np.zeros_like(z); g[2::3] = -1.0; return g\n\ndef ineq_boundary(z):\n    x, y, r = z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3]\n    return np.concatenate([x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r])\ndef jac_boundary(z):\n    J = np.zeros((4*N, 3*N));\n    for i in range(N):\n        xi, yi, ri =\
    \ 3*i, 3*i+1, 3*i+2\n        J[i, xi] = 1.0; J[i, ri] = -1.0; J[N+i, xi] = -1.0; J[N+i, ri] = -1.0\n        J[2*N+i, yi] = 1.0; J[2*N+i, ri] = -1.0; J[3*N+i, yi] = -1.0; J[3*N+i, ri] = -1.0\n    return J\n\ndef ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n    centers, r = z_to_cr(z)\n    diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n    dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1); return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\ndef jac_nonoverlap(z):\n    centers, _ = z_to_cr(z)\n    m = N*(N-1)//2; J = np.zeros((m, 3*N)); k = 0\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(i+1, N):\n            xi, yi, ri = 3*i, 3*i+1, 3*i+2; xj, yj, rj = 3*j, 3*j+1, 3*j+2\n            dx = centers[i,0] - centers[j,0]; dy = centers[i,1] - centers[j,1]\n            d = math.hypot(dx, dy); invd = 1.0 / d if d > 1e-12 else 0.0\n            J[k, xi] = dx * invd; J[k, yi] = dy * invd; J[k, ri] = -1.0\n            J[k, xj] = -dx * invd; J[k, yj] = -dy * invd; J[k, rj] = -1.0\n            k += 1\n    return\
    \ J\n\ndef _ensure_validity(centers, radii):\n    for i in range(N): radii[i] = min(radii[i], centers[i,0], 1-centers[i,0], centers[i,1], 1-centers[i,1])\n    for _ in range(10):\n        violations = 0\n        for i in range(N):\n            for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n                rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                if dist < rad_sum:\n                    violations += 1\n                    if rad_sum > 0: scale = (dist / rad_sum) * (1.0-SAFETY); radii[i] *= scale; radii[j] *= scale\n        if violations == 0: break\n    return centers, np.maximum(radii, 0)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    # Expanded set of hole locations and jitter amplitudes\n    hole_locations = [(x*0.2, y*0.2) for x in range(1,5) for y in range(1,5)] # 16 locations\n    jitter_amplitudes = [1.0e-3, 2.0e-3, 3.0e-3, 4.0e-3, 5.0e-3, 6.0e-3, 7.0e-3, 8.0e-3] # 8 levels\n    \n    best_score = -1\n    best_packing = (None, None)\n\
    \    \n    bounds = []\n    for i in range(N): bounds.extend([(0,1), (0,1), (R_MIN, 0.5)])\n    constraints = [\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary, 'jac': jac_boundary},\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap, 'jac': jac_nonoverlap},\n    ]\n\n    run_idx = 0\n    # Total runs: 16 * 8 = 128. This is a lot, so we reduce maxiter to compensate.\n    for hole_cx, hole_cy in hole_locations:\n        for jitter_amp in jitter_amplitudes:\n            run_idx += 1\n            seed = int(hole_cx*1000 + hole_cy*1000 + jitter_amp*10000) + run_idx + 4000\n            initial_z = _generate_seed(hole_cx, hole_cy, jitter_amp, seed)\n            \n            res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', jac=objective_jac,\n                           bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n                           options={'maxiter': 250, 'ftol': 1e-9}) # Reduced maxiter\n            \n            if res.success and -res.fun > best_score:\n                best_score\
    \ = -res.fun\n                centers, radii = z_to_cr(res.x)\n                best_packing = (centers, radii)\n\n    if best_packing[0] is None: return None, None\n\n    final_centers, final_radii = _ensure_validity(best_packing[0], best_packing[1])\n    return final_centers, final_radii\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 298` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 298 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID\
    \ | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 694 | 1 | Prometheus III: Replication of Lineage SOTA (Eval 620) | Prometheus III | 442 | 2.6359831 |\n| 662 | 1 | SOTA Deepening 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New 'Sparse' SOTA (Eval 641) | Prometheus II | 418 | 2.6359831 |\n| 654 | 1 | Utility: Export Contact Data for Prometheus II SOTA (Eval 620) | Prometheus II | 412 | 0.0000000 |\n| 652 | 1 | Hard Constraint Seeding 2 (Bugfix): Locking Pair (6, 12) | Prometheus II | 411 | 2.6250545 |\n| 650 | 1 | Hard Constraint Seeding 2: Locking Pair (6, 12) | Prometheus II | 410 | 0.0000000 |\n| 646 | 1 | Hard Constraint Deepening 1: Jitter Search on Locked Pair (8, 13) Packing | Prometheus II | 409 | 2.6359774 |\n| 643 | 1 | Hard Constraint Seeding 1: Locking Pair (8, 13) | Prometheus II | 408 | 2.6340736 |\n| 637 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 4: Targeting Mid-List Pair (1, 6) | Prometheus II | 404 | 2.6359831 |\n| 635 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 3: Targeting\
    \ Second-Closest Pair (16, 17) | Prometheus II | 403 | 2.6359831 |\n| 633 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 2: Targeting Closest Near-Contact (8, 13) | Prometheus II | 402 | 2.6359831 |\n\nPage 1 of 10 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-10, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
