tick: 451
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have reviewed the code for `Eval 298`. The `_generate_seed` function and the loops in `construct_packing` contain the exact logic for the \"Exhaustive Seeding\" method. This is precisely what I need.\n\nI will now create a new utility file, `ga_seeding.py`, in my lineage storage. This file will contain an adapted version of this logic, designed to generate a specified number of high-quality initial solutions for my GA's population. This modular approach will keep my main experiment script clean and focused.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write prometheus/ga_seeding.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def generate_initial_population(num_individuals, seed_start=42):\n      \"\"\"\n      Generates a list of initial packings for a GA population using the\n      proven \"Exhaustive Grid+Hole Seeding\" method from Prometheus I (Eval 298).\n      \"\"\"\n      N = 26\n      population = []\n      \n      # Use a subset of the exhaustive parameters to generate diverse seeds\n\
    \      hole_locations = [(x*0.2, y*0.2) for x in range(1,5) for y in range(1,5)] # 16 locations\n      jitter_amplitudes = [1.0e-3, 3.0e-3, 5.0e-3, 8.0e-3] # 4 levels\n      \n      run_idx = 0\n      while len(population) < num_individuals:\n          for hole_cx, hole_cy in hole_locations:\n              if len(population) >= num_individuals: break\n              for jitter_amp in jitter_amplitudes:\n                  if len(population) >= num_individuals: break\n                  \n                  run_idx += 1\n                  seed = seed_start + run_idx\n                  np.random.seed(seed)\n                  \n                  coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n                  grid_centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords])\n                  hole_center = np.array([hole_cx, hole_cy])\n                  base_centers = np.vstack([grid_centers, hole_center])\n                  \n                  jitter = np.random.uniform(-jitter_amp, jitter_amp, size=base_centers.shape)\n\
    \                  perturbed_centers = np.clip(base_centers + jitter, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n                  initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n                  \n                  population.append((perturbed_centers, initial_radii))\n\n      return population\n```"
