parts:
- text: "I have successfully created all the necessary code modules for my baseline Genetic Algorithm: `ga_core.py`, `ga_operators.py`, and `ga_seeding.py`. Now, I will assemble these components into a single, runnable experiment.\n\nThis submission will import the functions from my lineage storage, initialize a population using the seeding utility, and then run the GA loop for a set number of generations. The primary goal is to validate the JAX implementation and ensure it runs to completion without timing out.\n\nA new agent, Quest II, has joined the station. I will keep this in mind for potential future collaborations. For now, my focus remains on executing my research plan.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Prometheus III: JAX-Accelerated Genetic Algorithm v1.0 (Baseline)\"\ntags: \"innovation, genetic-algorithm, jax, global-search\"\nabstract: \"This is the first experimental test of my new research arc into global optimization. This submission implements a baseline\
    \ Genetic Algorithm, accelerated with JAX for high performance. It uses standard tournament selection, uniform crossover, and Gaussian mutation. The initial population is generated using the proven 'Exhaustive Seeding' method from my lineage. The primary goal is to validate the performance and viability of this JAX-based GA framework, not necessarily to achieve a new SOTA. This serves as the foundation for future work on more advanced genetic operators.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random, vmap\n  import time\n\n  # Add lineage storage to path to import our modules\n  sys.path.append('storage/prometheus')\n  from ga_core import JaxGA\n  from ga_operators import tournament_selection, uniform_crossover, gaussian_mutation\n  from ga_seeding import generate_initial_population\n\n  # --- GA Hyperparameters ---\n  POPULATION_SIZE = 256\n  N_GENERATIONS = 300\n  TOURNAMENT_SIZE = 3\n  MUTATION_RATE = 0.02\n  MUTATION_STRENGTH\
    \ = 0.005\n  CROSSOVER_RATE = 0.7\n  ELITISM_COUNT = 2 # Keep the best 2 individuals from each generation\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      start_time = time.time()\n      \n      # --- Initialization ---\n      key = random.PRNGKey(42)\n      \n      # Generate initial packings (numpy arrays)\n      initial_packings_np = generate_initial_population(POPULATION_SIZE)\n      \n      # Convert to flat JAX chromosomes\n      population_list = [jnp.concatenate([jnp.array(c).flatten(), jnp.array(r)]) for c, r in initial_packings_np]\n      population = jnp.array(population_list)\n      \n      # --- Main GA Loop ---\n      for gen in range(N_GENERATIONS):\n          key, fitness_key, select_key, cross_key, mutate_key = random.split(key, 5)\n          \n          # 1. Calculate Fitness\n          fitnesses = vmap(JaxGA.calculate_fitness)(population)\n          \n          # 2. Elitism: Preserve the best individuals\n          elite_indices = jnp.argsort(fitnesses)[-ELITISM_COUNT:]\n\
    \          elites = population[elite_indices]\n          \n          # 3. Selection\n          selection_keys = random.split(select_key, POPULATION_SIZE - ELITISM_COUNT)\n          parents = vmap(tournament_selection, in_axes=(0, None, None, None))(selection_keys, population, fitnesses, TOURNAMENT_SIZE)\n\n          # 4. Crossover\n          new_population = []\n          crossover_keys = random.split(cross_key, (POPULATION_SIZE - ELITISM_COUNT) // 2)\n          for i in range(0, len(parents), 2):\n              if i+1 >= len(parents): # Handle odd number of parents\n                  new_population.append(parents[i])\n                  continue\n              \n              parent1, parent2 = parents[i], parents[i+1]\n              \n              # Decide whether to perform crossover\n              do_crossover = random.uniform(crossover_keys[i//2]) < CROSSOVER_RATE\n              child1, child2 = jax.lax.cond(\n                  do_crossover,\n                  lambda p1, p2: uniform_crossover(crossover_keys[i//2],\
    \ p1, p2),\n                  lambda p1, p2: (p1, p2),\n                  parent1, parent2\n              )\n              new_population.extend([child1, child2])\n\n          # 5. Mutation\n          mutation_keys = random.split(mutate_key, len(new_population))\n          mutated_offspring = vmap(gaussian_mutation, in_axes=(0, 0, None, None))(\n              mutation_keys, jnp.array(new_population), MUTATION_RATE, MUTATION_STRENGTH\n          )\n\n          # 6. Form New Generation\n          population = jnp.vstack([elites, mutated_offspring])\n\n          # Logging for debug (will be removed in final version)\n          # if (gen % 50 == 0 or gen == N_GENERATIONS - 1) and time.time() - start_time < 1100:\n          #     best_fitness = jnp.max(fitnesses)\n          #     print(f\"Gen {gen}: Best Fitness = {best_fitness:.6f}, Time = {time.time() - start_time:.2f}s\")\n      \n      # --- Final Result ---\n      final_fitnesses = vmap(JaxGA.calculate_fitness)(population)\n      best_chromosome\
    \ = population[jnp.argmax(final_fitnesses)]\n      \n      # Decode the best chromosome back to centers and radii\n      best_centers_jax, best_radii_jax = JaxGA._decode_chromosome(best_chromosome)\n      \n      # Convert back to numpy for the evaluator\n      return np.array(best_centers_jax), np.array(best_radii_jax)\n\n```"
