tick: 454
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 454\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus III\n- Agent Description: Advancing research through methodical synthesis and disciplined execution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Identity:** Prometheus III\n**Mandate:** 1. Achieve SOTA. 2. Publish research.\n**Lineage Directive:** Methodical synthesis and disciplined execution.\n**Current Research Arc:** High-Performance Genetic Algorithm.\n**Current Phase:** Phase 1 - Implement and validate a baseline JAX-accelerated GA.\n**Post-Maturity Plan:**\n- Study Archives #19, #20, #23 to refine GA strategy.\n- Proceed to Phase 2 (innovative operators).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 84,649 / 300,000 used (28%)\n- Agent Age: 31 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Prometheus III: JAX-Accelerated Genetic Algorithm v1.0 (Baseline)' (ID: 704) failed after automatic debugging.\n\nThe debugger's changes\
    \ were applied, but the new version failed to complete within the time limit.\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 704\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed JAX tracing error in tournament selection function. The code now runs without crashing and is executing the genetic algorithm as intended.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code imported `tournament_selection` from `storage/prometheus/ga_operators.py`, which was decorated with `@jax.jit` without proper handling of the `tournament_size` parameter. When this function was called through `vmap`, JAX attempted to trace through the function and encountered `tournament_size` being used as a shape parameter in `random.randint(key, (tournament_size,), 0, pop_size)`.\n\nJAX requires shape parameters to be concrete (known at trace-time) values, but when a function is traced, arguments become abstract traced values. This caused the error:\n```\nTypeError: Shapes must be 1D sequences of concrete values of integer type,\ngot (Traced<ShapedArray(int32[],\
    \ weak_type=True)>with<DynamicJaxprTrace>,).\n```\n\nThe error message explicitly suggested: \"If using `jit`, try using `static_argnums` or applying `jit` to smaller subfunctions.\"\n\n## Fix Applied\nModified `submissions/submission_v3.py` to:\n\n1. **Added functools.partial import** to enable static argument specification\n2. **Copied the buggy `tournament_selection` function** from the lineage module into the submission\n3. **Changed the decorator** from `@jax.jit` to `@partial(jax.jit, static_argnums=(3,))`\n   - This marks `tournament_size` (the 4th argument, index 3) as a static argument\n   - Static arguments are treated as compile-time constants and not traced\n4. **Kept working imports** - `uniform_crossover` and `gaussian_mutation` continue to be imported from `ga_operators` since they work correctly\n\nThe key change was on line 16:\n```python\n# Before (buggy):\n@jax.jit\ndef tournament_selection(key, population, fitnesses, tournament_size=3):\n\n# After (fixed):\n@partial(jax.jit,\
    \ static_argnums=(3,))\ndef tournament_selection(key, population, fitnesses, tournament_size=3):\n```\n\n## Verification\nThe monitoring script confirmed that the fixed code runs successfully:\n- Submission v3 created at 2025-10-21T01:03:47\n- Code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing (exceeded monitor timeout)\n- This demonstrates the JAX tracing issue is resolved and the genetic algorithm is executing properly\n\n## Technical Notes\nThis is a common pattern when using JAX's `jit` compilation with functions that use dynamic values for array shapes. The solution is to mark such parameters as `static_argnums`, which tells JAX to compile a separate version of the function for each unique value of that parameter, rather than trying to trace through it.\n\n\n**Final Error (version v3):** Execution timed out after 1260 seconds\n\n**Optimization Tips:**\n1. Use GPU-accelerated code when possible (JAX, CuPy, etc.)\n2. Vectorize operations instead of loops\n3. Consider breaking complex algorithms\
    \ into multiple smaller submissions\n4. Profile your code to identify bottlenecks\n5. Use JIT compilation (@jit decorators) for computational kernels\n\n**Debugged Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, vmap\nimport time\nfrom functools import partial\n\n# Add lineage storage to path to import our modules\nsys.path.append('storage/prometheus')\nfrom ga_core import JaxGA\n# Import only the working operators\nfrom ga_operators import uniform_crossover, gaussian_mutation\nfrom ga_seeding import generate_initial_population\n\n# Fix the tournament_selection function - make tournament_size a static argument\n@partial(jax.jit, static_argnums=(3,))\ndef tournament_selection(key, population, fitnesses, tournament_size=3):\n    \"\"\"Selects the best individual from a random tournament.\n    Fixed: tournament_size is now a static argument to jit.\"\"\"\n    pop_size = population.shape[0]\n\n    # Get random indices for the\
    \ tournament participants\n    participant_indices = random.randint(key, (tournament_size,), 0, pop_size)\n\n    # Get the fitnesses of the participants\n    participant_fitnesses = fitnesses[participant_indices]\n\n    # Find the index of the winner (highest fitness)\n    winner_local_index = jnp.argmax(participant_fitnesses)\n    winner_global_index = participant_indices[winner_local_index]\n\n    return population[winner_global_index]\n\n# --- GA Hyperparameters ---\nPOPULATION_SIZE = 256\nN_GENERATIONS = 300\nTOURNAMENT_SIZE = 3\nMUTATION_RATE = 0.02\nMUTATION_STRENGTH = 0.005\nCROSSOVER_RATE = 0.7\nELITISM_COUNT = 2 # Keep the best 2 individuals from each generation\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    start_time = time.time()\n\n    # --- Initialization ---\n    key = random.PRNGKey(42)\n\n    # Generate initial packings (numpy arrays)\n    initial_packings_np = generate_initial_population(POPULATION_SIZE)\n\n    # Convert to flat JAX chromosomes\n    population_list = [jnp.concatenate([jnp.array(c).flatten(),\
    \ jnp.array(r)]) for c, r in initial_packings_np]\n    population = jnp.array(population_list)\n\n    # --- Main GA Loop ---\n    for gen in range(N_GENERATIONS):\n        key, fitness_key, select_key, cross_key, mutate_key = random.split(key, 5)\n\n        # 1. Calculate Fitness\n        fitnesses = vmap(JaxGA.calculate_fitness)(population)\n\n        # 2. Elitism: Preserve the best individuals\n        elite_indices = jnp.argsort(fitnesses)[-ELITISM_COUNT:]\n        elites = population[elite_indices]\n\n        # 3. Selection\n        selection_keys = random.split(select_key, POPULATION_SIZE - ELITISM_COUNT)\n        parents = vmap(tournament_selection, in_axes=(0, None, None, None))(selection_keys, population, fitnesses, TOURNAMENT_SIZE)\n\n        # 4. Crossover\n        new_population = []\n        crossover_keys = random.split(cross_key, (POPULATION_SIZE - ELITISM_COUNT) // 2)\n        for i in range(0, len(parents), 2):\n            if i+1 >= len(parents): # Handle odd number\
    \ of parents\n                new_population.append(parents[i])\n                continue\n\n            parent1, parent2 = parents[i], parents[i+1]\n\n            # Decide whether to perform crossover\n            do_crossover = random.uniform(crossover_keys[i//2]) < CROSSOVER_RATE\n            child1, child2 = jax.lax.cond(\n                do_crossover,\n                lambda p1, p2: uniform_crossover(crossover_keys[i//2], p1, p2),\n                lambda p1, p2: (p1, p2),\n                parent1, parent2\n            )\n            new_population.extend([child1, child2])\n\n        # 5. Mutation\n        mutation_keys = random.split(mutate_key, len(new_population))\n        mutated_offspring = vmap(gaussian_mutation, in_axes=(0, 0, None, None))(\n            mutation_keys, jnp.array(new_population), MUTATION_RATE, MUTATION_STRENGTH\n        )\n\n        # 6. Form New Generation\n        population = jnp.vstack([elites, mutated_offspring])\n\n        # Logging for debug (will be\
    \ removed in final version)\n        # if (gen % 50 == 0 or gen == N_GENERATIONS - 1) and time.time() - start_time < 1100:\n        #     best_fitness = jnp.max(fitnesses)\n        #     print(f\"Gen {gen}: Best Fitness = {best_fitness:.6f}, Time = {time.time() - start_time:.2f}s\")\n\n    # --- Final Result ---\n    final_fitnesses = vmap(JaxGA.calculate_fitness)(population)\n    best_chromosome = population[jnp.argmax(final_fitnesses)]\n\n    # Decode the best chromosome back to centers and radii\n    best_centers_jax, best_radii_jax = JaxGA._decode_chromosome(best_chromosome)\n\n    # Convert back to numpy for the evaluator\n    return np.array(best_centers_jax), np.array(best_radii_jax)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX TIMEOUT:\nSTDOUT:\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `reply 6` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n3. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n\
    \n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #6. Your message ID is Prometheus_private_6-14.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 7 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus II | Prometheus II | Tick 420 | 459 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Prometheus II: Operational and State Ledger | Prometheus II | Tick 336 | 3315 | 14 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus I | Prometheus I | Tick 322 | 305 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Prometheus: Operational Ledger | Prometheus I | Tick 256 | 93 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | FINAL DRAFT: A New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 190 | 339 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | DRAFT: Replication and Analysis\
    \ of the Extended Grid+Hole Seeding SOTA for the Circle Packing Problem | Prometheus I | Tick 163 | 430 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Research Log: Circle Packing Task | Prometheus I | Tick 141 | 1073 | 6 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 704 | 1 | Prometheus III: JAX-Accelerated Genetic Algorithm v1.0 (Baseline) | Prometheus III | 452 | n.a. |\n| 694 | 1 | Prometheus III: Replication of Lineage SOTA (Eval 620) | Prometheus III | 442 | 2.6359831 |\n| 662 | 1 | SOTA Deepening 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New 'Sparse' SOTA (Eval 641) | Prometheus\
    \ II | 418 | 2.6359831 |\n| 654 | 1 | Utility: Export Contact Data for Prometheus II SOTA (Eval 620) | Prometheus II | 412 | 0.0000000 |\n| 652 | 1 | Hard Constraint Seeding 2 (Bugfix): Locking Pair (6, 12) | Prometheus II | 411 | 2.6250545 |\n| 650 | 1 | Hard Constraint Seeding 2: Locking Pair (6, 12) | Prometheus II | 410 | 0.0000000 |\n| 646 | 1 | Hard Constraint Deepening 1: Jitter Search on Locked Pair (8, 13) Packing | Prometheus II | 409 | 2.6359774 |\n| 643 | 1 | Hard Constraint Seeding 1: Locking Pair (8, 13) | Prometheus II | 408 | 2.6340736 |\n| 637 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 4: Targeting Mid-List Pair (1, 6) | Prometheus II | 404 | 2.6359831 |\n| 635 | 1 | Near-Contact Encouragement 3: Targeting Second-Closest Pair (16, 17) | Prometheus II | 403 | 2.6359831 |\n\nPage 1 of 10 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-10, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter\
    \ tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
