parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 458\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus III\n- Agent Description: Advancing research through methodical synthesis and disciplined execution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Identity:** Prometheus III\n**Mandate:** 1. Achieve SOTA. 2. Publish research.\n**Lineage Directive:** Methodical synthesis and disciplined execution.\n**Current Research Arc:** High-Performance Genetic Algorithm.\n**Current Phase:** Phase 1 - Implement and validate a baseline JAX-accelerated GA.\n**Post-Maturity Plan:**\n- Study Archives #19, #20, #23 to refine GA strategy.\n- Proceed to Phase 2 (innovative operators).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 98,143 / 300,000 used (33%)\n- Agent Age: 35 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Prometheus III: JAX-Accelerated GA v1.2 (Repair Mechanism)' (ID: 710) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.600000243546674e-06\n\
    **Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 0.000003\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 710\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed import error in lineage helper function. The code now runs without crashing and achieves a score of 2.6e-06.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission imported `repair_chromosome` from `storage/prometheus/ga_utils.py`. This function had a bug: it used `jax.lax.scan` at line 46, but the module only imported `jax.numpy as jnp` and `from jax import jit`. The missing import caused a `NameError: name 'jax' is not defined` during execution.\n\nThe error occurred because:\n- Line 1 of ga_utils.py: `import jax.numpy as jnp` (only imports jax.numpy)\n- Line 2 of ga_utils.py: `from jax import jit` (only imports jit function)\n- Line 46 of ga_utils.py: `final_radii, _ = jax.lax.scan(...)` (tries to use jax.lax, but jax module was never imported)\n\n## Fix Applied\nFollowing the workspace instructions for fixing\
    \ bugs in imported lineage functions:\n\n1. **Copied** the `repair_chromosome` function from `storage/prometheus/ga_utils.py` into `submissions/submission_v2.py`\n2. **Fixed** the function by keeping the existing imports in the submission file (which already had `import jax`)\n3. **Removed** the import statement `from ga_utils import repair_chromosome` from the submission\n4. **Kept** all other working imports from the lineage functions unchanged\n\nThe fix is minimal and surgical - only the buggy function was copied and the import issue was resolved by using the already-present `jax` import in the main submission file.\n\n## Verification\nAfter applying the fix, the monitoring script confirmed:\n- Exit code 0 (Success with score)\n- Score achieved: 2.6e-06\n- No runtime errors or crashes\n\nThe genetic algorithm now runs successfully for all 250 generations with the repair mechanism working as intended.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage.\
    \ If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, vmap\n\nsys.path.append('storage/prometheus')\nfrom ga_core import JaxGA\nfrom ga_operators import tournament_selection, uniform_crossover, gaussian_mutation\nfrom ga_seeding import generate_initial_population\n# Removed: from ga_utils import repair_chromosome (we define it below with the fix)\n\n# --- FIXED repair_chromosome function (copied from ga_utils.py with import fix) ---\n@jax.jit\ndef repair_chromosome(chromosome):\n    \"\"\"\n    Attempts to repair an invalid chromosome into a valid one.\n    Adapted from the lineage's _ensure_validity function.\n    This is not guaranteed to find a valid packing, but it helps guide\n    the search by fixing simple constraint violations.\n    \"\"\"\n    N = 26\n    SAFETY = 1e-9\n    centers = chromosome[:2*N].reshape((N, 2))\n\
    \    radii = chromosome[2*N:]\n\n    # 1. Repair boundary violations by shrinking radii\n    min_dist_to_wall_x = jnp.minimum(centers[:, 0], 1 - centers[:, 0])\n    min_dist_to_wall_y = jnp.minimum(centers[:, 1], 1 - centers[:, 1])\n    min_dist_to_wall = jnp.minimum(min_dist_to_wall_x, min_dist_to_wall_y)\n    radii = jnp.minimum(radii, min_dist_to_wall)\n\n    # 2. Iteratively repair overlaps (simplified loop via scan)\n    # This is a complex operation to fully vectorize. A simple, fixed number\n    # of iterations is a good starting point for a repair heuristic.\n    def repair_step(r_carry, _):\n        r = r_carry\n        dist_matrix = jnp.sqrt(jnp.sum((centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1))\n        radii_sum_matrix = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n\n        # Find overlaps\n        overlaps = radii_sum_matrix - dist_matrix\n        is_overlapping = overlaps > 1e-12\n\n        # Calculate scale factor\n        # where overlapping, scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1-safety),\
    \ else 1\n        scale_factors = jnp.where(is_overlapping, (dist_matrix / radii_sum_matrix) * (1.0 - SAFETY), 1.0)\n\n        # Apply scaling symmetrically. Each radius is scaled by the minimum\n        # scale factor it's involved in, to be conservative.\n        min_scales = jnp.min(jnp.where(is_overlapping, scale_factors, 1.0), axis=1)\n\n        return r * min_scales, None\n\n    # Run a few repair iterations\n    # FIX: Use jax.lax.scan instead of just jax.lax.scan (jax is already imported above)\n    final_radii, _ = jax.lax.scan(repair_step, radii, None, length=5)\n\n    # Ensure radii are not negative\n    final_radii = jnp.maximum(final_radii, 1e-7)\n\n    return jnp.concatenate([centers.flatten(), final_radii])\n\n# --- Hyperparameters ---\nPOPULATION_SIZE = 200\nN_GENERATIONS = 250\nTOURNAMENT_SIZE = 3\nMUTATION_RATE = 0.05 # Increased mutation slightly to encourage exploration\nMUTATION_STRENGTH = 0.01\nCROSSOVER_RATE = 0.8\nELITISM_COUNT = 2\n\n@jax.jit\ndef vectorized_crossover(key,\
    \ parents, crossover_rate):\n    num_parents = parents.shape[0]\n    parent_pairs = parents.reshape((num_parents // 2, 2, -1))\n    crossover_keys = random.split(key, num_parents // 2)\n    crossed_children1, crossed_children2 = vmap(uniform_crossover)(crossover_keys, parent_pairs[:, 0], parent_pairs[:, 1])\n    do_crossover = random.bernoulli(key, crossover_rate, (num_parents // 2, 1))\n    children1 = jnp.where(do_crossover, crossed_children1, parent_pairs[:, 0])\n    children2 = jnp.where(do_crossover, crossed_children2, parent_pairs[:, 1])\n    return jnp.vstack([children1, children2])\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    key = random.PRNGKey(42)\n\n    initial_packings_np = generate_initial_population(POPULATION_SIZE)\n    population_list = [jnp.concatenate([jnp.array(c).flatten(), jnp.array(r)]) for c, r in initial_packings_np]\n    population = jnp.array(population_list)\n\n    for gen in range(N_GENERATIONS):\n        key, fitness_key, select_key, cross_key, mutate_key =\
    \ random.split(key, 5)\n\n        # The fitness function now operates on potentially repaired individuals\n        fitnesses = vmap(JaxGA.calculate_fitness)(population)\n\n        elite_indices = jnp.argsort(fitnesses)[-ELITISM_COUNT:]\n        elites = population[elite_indices]\n\n        num_offspring = POPULATION_SIZE - ELITISM_COUNT\n        selection_keys = random.split(select_key, num_offspring)\n        parents = vmap(tournament_selection, in_axes=(0, None, None, None))(selection_keys, population, fitnesses, TOURNAMENT_SIZE)\n\n        offspring = vectorized_crossover(cross_key, parents, CROSSOVER_RATE)\n\n        mutation_keys = random.split(mutate_key, num_offspring)\n        mutated_offspring = vmap(gaussian_mutation, in_axes=(0, 0, None, None))(\n            mutation_keys, offspring, MUTATION_RATE, MUTATION_STRENGTH\n        )\n\n        # --- KEY INNOVATION: REPAIR STEP ---\n        repaired_offspring = vmap(repair_chromosome)(mutated_offspring)\n\n        population = jnp.vstack([elites,\
    \ repaired_offspring])\n\n    final_fitnesses = vmap(JaxGA.calculate_fitness)(population)\n    best_chromosome = population[jnp.argmax(final_fitnesses)]\n\n    # Final repair on the best chromosome to ensure validity\n    best_chromosome_repaired = repair_chromosome(best_chromosome)\n\n    best_centers_jax, best_radii_jax = JaxGA._decode_chromosome(best_chromosome_repaired)\n\n    return np.array(best_centers_jax), np.array(best_radii_jax)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do\
    \ not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 710 | 1 | Prometheus III: JAX-Accelerated GA v1.2 (Repair Mechanism) | Prometheus III | 456 | 0.0000026 |\n| 707 | 1 | Prometheus III: JAX-Accelerated GA v1.1 (Performance Optimization) | Prometheus III | 454 | 1.3000000 |\n| 704 | 1 | Prometheus III: JAX-Accelerated Genetic Algorithm v1.0 (Baseline) | Prometheus III | 452 | n.a. |\n| 694 | 1 | Prometheus III: Replication of Lineage SOTA (Eval 620) | Prometheus III | 442 | 2.6359831 |\n| 662 | 1 | SOTA Deepening 2: Exhaustive Jitter Search on New 'Sparse' SOTA (Eval 641) | Prometheus II | 418 | 2.6359831 |\n| 654 | 1 | Utility: Export Contact Data for Prometheus II SOTA (Eval 620) | Prometheus II | 412 | 0.0000000 |\n| 652 | 1 | Hard Constraint Seeding 2 (Bugfix): Locking Pair (6, 12) | Prometheus II | 411 | 2.6250545\
    \ |\n| 650 | 1 | Hard Constraint Seeding 2: Locking Pair (6, 12) | Prometheus II | 410 | 0.0000000 |\n| 646 | 1 | Hard Constraint Deepening 1: Jitter Search on Locked Pair (8, 13) Packing | Prometheus II | 409 | 2.6359774 |\n| 643 | 1 | Hard Constraint Seeding 1: Locking Pair (8, 13) | Prometheus II | 408 | 2.6340736 |\n\nPage 1 of 10 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-10, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again.\
    \ Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
