tick: 462
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am in the Research Counter. My plan is now in the execution phase. The first step is to create the missing piece for my \"Seed-Nudge-Refine\" pipeline: a utility function to identify the best near-contact pair to \"nudge\".\n\nI will add this function to my `ga_utils.py` file, as it is a general-purpose utility that could be useful in the future. This function will take a packing and find the pair of non-touching circles with the smallest gap between them, which will be the target for the \"nudge\" stage.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write prometheus/ga_utils.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import numpy as np\n  from jax import jit\n  from scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\n\n  # ... (previous repair_chromosome function) ...\n  @jit\n  def repair_chromosome(chromosome):\n      \"\"\"\n      Attempts to repair an invalid chromosome into a valid one.\n      Adapted from the lineage's _ensure_validity function.\n      FIXED: Added\
    \ full jax import.\n      \"\"\"\n      N = 26\n      SAFETY = 1e-9\n      centers = chromosome[:2*N].reshape((N, 2))\n      radii = chromosome[2*N:]\n\n      min_dist_to_wall_x = jnp.minimum(centers[:, 0], 1 - centers[:, 0])\n      min_dist_to_wall_y = jnp.minimum(centers[:, 1], 1 - centers[:, 1])\n      min_dist_to_wall = jnp.minimum(min_dist_to_wall_x, min_dist_to_wall_y)\n      radii = jnp.minimum(radii, min_dist_to_wall)\n      \n      def repair_step(r_carry, _):\n          r = r_carry\n          dist_matrix = jnp.sqrt(jnp.sum((centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1))\n          radii_sum_matrix = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n          overlaps = radii_sum_matrix - dist_matrix\n          is_overlapping = overlaps > 1e-12\n          scale_factors = jnp.where(is_overlapping, (dist_matrix / radii_sum_matrix) * (1.0 - SAFETY), 1.0)\n          min_scales = jnp.min(jnp.where(is_overlapping, scale_factors, 1.0), axis=1)\n          return r * min_scales, None\n\n      final_radii,\
    \ _ = jax.lax.scan(repair_step, radii, None, length=5)\n      final_radii = jnp.maximum(final_radii, 1e-7)\n\n      return jnp.concatenate([centers.flatten(), final_radii])\n\n  def find_closest_near_contact(centers, radii, slack_threshold=0.01):\n      \"\"\"\n      Finds the pair of non-touching circles with the smallest gap.\n      Uses numpy/scipy as this is a pre-processing step, not a performance bottleneck.\n      \"\"\"\n      N = centers.shape[0]\n      dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n      \n      min_slack = float('inf')\n      best_pair = None\n      \n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N):\n              slack = dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j])\n              # Check for a small positive slack\n              if 1e-9 < slack < min_slack:\n                  min_slack = slack\n                  best_pair = (i, j)\n      \n      # Fallback if no near-contact is found within the tight threshold\n      if best_pair is None:\n         \
    \ # Find any smallest positive slack\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  slack = dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j])\n                  if slack > 1e-9 and slack < min_slack:\n                      min_slack = slack\n                      best_pair = (i, j)\n\n      return best_pair\n```"
