tick: 463
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully added the `find_closest_near_contact` utility function to my storage. All the necessary code components for my \"Seed-Nudge-Refine\" pipeline are now in place.\n\nI will now assemble them into a single, cohesive experiment. This submission will be the culmination of my reflection and strategic pivot. It will:\n1.  Generate a pool of initial seeds.\n2.  For each seed, identify the best pair to nudge and run a short \"nudge\" optimization.\n3.  For each resulting \"nudged\" packing, run a full, deep \"refine\" optimization.\n4.  Return the best result from the entire process.\n\nThis is a computationally intensive process, so I will start with a modest number of seeds (16) to ensure it completes within the time limit.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Prometheus III: Seed-Nudge-Refine Pipeline v1.0\"\ntags: \"synthesis, pipeline, nudging, slsqp, seeding\"\nabstract: \"This experiment implements my new research strategy, the 'Seed-Nudge-Refine' pipeline,\
    \ which synthesizes the most successful methods of my lineage. It starts with a broad exploration via Exhaustive Seeding (Prometheus I), then applies a guided exploration step by dynamically identifying and 'nudging' the closest near-contact pair for each seed (Prometheus II/Scientia II), and finally performs a deep exploitation with a full SLSQP refinement on each candidate. This is a systematic test of the hypothesis that a multi-stage synthesis is superior to any single method.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import time\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/prometheus')\n  # NOTE: I am not using my GA modules for this experiment\n  from ga_seeding import generate_initial_population\n  from ga_utils import find_closest_near_contact\n\n  # --- Constants and Helper Functions ---\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n\n  def cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\n  def z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2),\
    \ z[N*2:]\n\n  def _ensure_validity(c, r):\n      for i in range(N): r[i] = min(r[i], c[i,0], 1-c[i,0], c[i,1], 1-c[i,1])\n      for _ in range(5): # Fewer iterations for speed\n          violations = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                  rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                  if dist < rad_sum:\n                      violations+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY); r[i]*=scale; r[j]*=scale\n          if violations == 0: break\n      return c, np.maximum(r, 0)\n\n  # --- Pipeline Configuration ---\n  NUM_SEEDS = 16\n  \n  # --- Stage 2: Nudge ---\n  def nudge_objective(z, encourage_pair):\n      centers, radii = z_to_cr(z)\n      base_objective = -np.sum(radii)\n      i, j = encourage_pair\n      dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n      target_dist = radii[i] + radii[j] + 0.005 # EPS_CLOSE\n      penalty = 1e2 * max(0, dist - target_dist)**2 # ALPHA_ENCOURAGE\n\
    \      return base_objective + penalty\n\n  # --- Stage 3: Refine ---\n  def refine_objective(z):\n      return -np.sum(z[N*2:])\n\n  def ineq_boundary(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\n\n  def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n      dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n      return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      start_time = time.time()\n      \n      # --- Stage 1: Seed ---\n      initial_packings = generate_initial_population(NUM_SEEDS)\n      \n      best_score = -1\n      best_packing = (None, None)\n      \n      bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n      constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n      for i, (centers_seed, radii_seed) in enumerate(initial_packings):\n          # Safety check\
    \ for time\n          if time.time() - start_time > 1150:\n              break\n\n          # --- Stage 2: Nudge ---\n          # First, refine the seed slightly to get a valid starting point for nudging\n          initial_z = cr_to_z(centers_seed, radii_seed)\n          res_pre_nudge = minimize(refine_objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 50, 'ftol': 1e-7})\n          c_pre, r_pre = z_to_cr(res_pre_nudge.x)\n\n          encourage_pair = find_closest_near_contact(c_pre, r_pre)\n          if encourage_pair is None:\n              # If no pair is found, just use the pre-nudged result\n              nudged_z = res_pre_nudge.x\n          else:\n              res_nudge = minimize(lambda z: nudge_objective(z, encourage_pair), res_pre_nudge.x, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 200, 'ftol': 1e-8})\n              nudged_z = res_nudge.x\n          \n          # --- Stage 3: Refine ---\n      \
    \    res_refine = minimize(refine_objective, nudged_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n          \n          current_score = -res_refine.fun\n          if res_refine.success and current_score > best_score:\n              best_score = current_score\n              best_packing = z_to_cr(res_refine.x)\n\n      if best_packing[0] is None:\n          # Fallback in case of total failure\n          c_fallback, r_fallback = generate_initial_population(1)[0]\n          return _ensure_validity(c_fallback, r_fallback)\n\n      return _ensure_validity(best_packing[0], best_packing[1])\n```"
