tick: 467
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have updated my operational ledger. I will now return to the Research Counter to submit the next iteration of my pipeline experiment, focusing on increased search breadth.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Prometheus III: Seed-Nudge-Refine Pipeline v1.2 (Wide Search)\"\ntags: \"synthesis, pipeline, nudging, slsqp, seeding, tuning, breadth-search\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests the hypothesis that search breadth is more critical than depth for the 'Seed-Nudge-Refine' pipeline. Based on the positive trend from Eval 724, this version dramatically increases the number of initial seeds from 16 to 48. To manage runtime, the final refinement stage's max iterations are reduced. The goal is to more thoroughly explore the solution space in the hope that one of the many nudged candidates will fall into a superior basin of attraction.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import\
    \ time\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/prometheus')\n  from ga_seeding import generate_initial_population\n  from ga_utils import find_closest_near_contact\n\n  # --- Constants and Helper Functions ---\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n\n  def cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\n  def z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\n  def _ensure_validity(c, r):\n      for i in range(N): r[i] = min(r[i], c[i,0], 1-c[i,0], c[i,1], 1-c[i,1])\n      for _ in range(5):\n          violations = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                  rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                  if dist < rad_sum:\n                      violations+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY); r[i]*=scale; r[j]*=scale\n          if violations == 0: break\n      return c, np.maximum(r, 0)\n\n  # --- Pipeline Configuration ---\n  NUM_SEEDS = 48 # Increased breadth\n  \n  # --- Stage\
    \ 2: Nudge ---\n  def nudge_objective(z, encourage_pair):\n      centers, radii = z_to_cr(z)\n      base_objective = -np.sum(radii)\n      i, j = encourage_pair\n      dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n      target_dist = radii[i] + radii[j] + 0.005\n      penalty = 1e2 * max(0, dist - target_dist)**2\n      return base_objective + penalty\n\n  # --- Stage 3: Refine ---\n  def refine_objective(z):\n      return -np.sum(z[N*2:])\n\n  def ineq_boundary(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\n\n  def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n      c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n      dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n      return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      start_time = time.time()\n      \n      initial_packings = generate_initial_population(NUM_SEEDS)\n      \n      best_score = -1\n     \
    \ best_packing = (None, None)\n      \n      bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n      constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n      for i, (centers_seed, radii_seed) in enumerate(initial_packings):\n          if time.time() - start_time > 1170: # Small safety margin\n              break\n\n          initial_z = cr_to_z(centers_seed, radii_seed)\n          encourage_pair = find_closest_near_contact(centers_seed, radii_seed)\n          \n          if encourage_pair is None:\n              nudged_z = initial_z\n          else:\n              res_nudge = minimize(lambda z: nudge_objective(z, encourage_pair), initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 250, 'ftol': 1e-8})\n              nudged_z = res_nudge.x\n          \n          # Reduced maxiter to compensate for more seeds\n          res_refine = minimize(refine_objective, nudged_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\
    \ options={'maxiter': 400, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n          \n          current_score = -res_refine.fun\n          if res_refine.success and current_score > best_score:\n              best_score = current_score\n              best_packing = z_to_cr(res_refine.x)\n\n      if best_packing[0] is None:\n          c_fallback, r_fallback = generate_initial_population(1)[0]\n          return _ensure_validity(c_fallback, r_fallback)\n\n      return _ensure_validity(best_packing[0], best_packing[1])\n```"
