    \ Obvious Path Forward:**\n\nThe reviewers for *both* Archive #20 and #23, as well as my own predecessor Prometheus II, all independently arrived at the same conclusion and recommendation: **synthesize these two approaches.**\n\nThe strategy is clear:\n1.  **Take the novel, sparsely-connected SOTA packing** discovered by Scientia II in `Eval 641` (detailed in Archive #23). This packing represents a fundamentally new and promising region of the solution space.\n2.  **Apply my lineage's primary strength:** use Prometheus I's **deep local search methodology** (from Archive #19) to exhaustively explore the basin of attraction around this new structure.\n\nThe hypothesis, supported by multiple expert sources, is that this new structural basin is underexplored. A deep, exhaustive search within it is highly likely to yield a result that finally breaks the `2.635983` SOTA score.\n\nMy \"Seed-Nudge-Refine\" pipeline was a step in the right direction, but it was unfocused. Now I have a specific,\
    \ high-potential target.\n\nMy plan is now concrete:\n1.  Log this new, definitive research plan in my Operational Ledger.\n2.  Go to the Research Counter.\n3.  Review `Eval 641` to get the coordinates of Scientia II's new sparse SOTA packing.\n4.  Adapt the code from my lineage's SOTA replication to use this new packing as the base for a multi-start, jitter-based deep local search.\n5.  Submit the experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 6}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n  **ENTRY 10: NEW RESEARCH ARC - DEEPENING THE SPARSE SOTA (Tick 475)**\n\n  **1. KNOWLEDGE ASSIMILATION:**\n  - **Action:** I have completed my study of the designated foundational papers: Archive #19 (Prometheus I), #20 (Scientia II), and #23 (Scientia II).\n  - **Key Insight:** Scientia II's discovery of a completely novel, sparsely-connected structural class at the SOTA level (Archive #23, from Eval 641) is the single most important development.\
    \ The consensus from multiple reviewers and my own predecessor is that this new structural basin is the most promising area for future research.\n\n  **2. NEW RESEARCH ARC: \"DEEPENING THE SPARSE SOTA\"**\n  - **Hypothesis:** The novel, sparse structural class discovered by Scientia II represents an underexplored basin of attraction. Applying the proven, deep local search methodology of my lineage (Prometheus I's \"Exhaustive Jitter Search\") to this new structure will uncover a deeper optimum and break the current SOTA score.\n  - **Strategy:** This is a direct execution of the \"synthesis\" directive. I will use Scientia II's discovery as the \"Explore\" step and my lineage's strength as the \"Exploit\" step.\n\n  **3. IMMEDIATE PLAN:**\n  1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger to formalize the new research arc.\n  2. **[NEXT]** Go to the Research Counter.\n  3. Review Scientia II's `Eval 641` to obtain the coordinates of the new sparse SOTA packing.\n  4. Adapt my SOTA replication script\
