- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 479\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus III\n- Agent Description: Advancing research through methodical synthesis and disciplined execution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Identity:** Prometheus III\n**Mandate:** 1. Achieve SOTA. 2. Publish research.\n**Lineage Directive:** Methodical synthesis and disciplined execution.\n**Current Research Arc:** Deepening the Sparse SOTA.\n**Plan:**\n1. [DONE] Locate sparse SOTA packing data from Eval 641.\n2. [NEXT] Read the packing data from Scientia II's storage.\n3. Submit a \"Jitter Search\" experiment on this new packing.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 154,816 / 300,000 used (52%)\n- Agent Age: 56 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Prometheus III: Deepening the Sparse\
    \ SOTA (Scientia II, Eval 641)' (ID: 749) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.6359773925176815\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635977\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 749\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the ValueError that prevented code execution. The submission now runs successfully and achieves a score of 2.636.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a seed value overflow error on line 53:\n```python\nnp.random.seed(int(time.time()*1000) + i)\n```\n\nThe issue: When `time.time()` (a Unix timestamp around 1.7 billion seconds) is multiplied by 1000 and converted to an integer, it produces a value like `1,729,000,000,000` or higher. NumPy's `random.seed()` function only accepts seed values between 0 and `2**32 - 1` (approximately 4.3 billion). The calculated seed exceeded this maximum, causing a `ValueError`.\n\n## Fix Applied\nModified line 53 in `submissions/submission_v2.py` to use modulo\
    \ operation:\n```python\nnp.random.seed((int(time.time()*1000) + i) % (2**32))\n```\n\nThis ensures the seed value always stays within the valid range [0, 2^32-1] by wrapping around using modulo arithmetic.\n\n## Result\n- **Status**: Code executes successfully without crashes\n- **Score**: 2.636 (circle packing area sum)\n- **Approach**: Multi-start SLSQP optimization with jittered initialization from Scientia II's sparse SOTA configuration\n- **Verification**: Confirmed via monitor_evaluation.py (exit code 0)\n\nThe fix was minimal and surgical - only the seed calculation needed adjustment. All other logic remains intact and functional.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport time\n\n# --- Constants ---\nN = 26\nR_MIN = 1e-6\nSAFETY = 1e-9\n\n# --- Sparse\
    \ SOTA Packing from Scientia II (Eval 641) ---\nSPARSE_SOTA_CENTERS = np.array([\n    [8.468730125805343234e-02, 8.468730125830406519e-02], [1.323600942410112502e-01, 2.964345012445476768e-01],\n    [7.826927088834340074e-02, 5.000000000003786971e-01], [1.323600942404387637e-01, 7.035654987557696805e-01],\n    [8.468730125807956421e-02, 9.153126987420653338e-01], [2.735316496508346518e-01, 1.052760785560242357e-01],\n    [3.811250649552991310e-01, 2.991123313402994088e-01], [2.697939589748069578e-01, 5.000000000007415180e-01],\n    [3.811250649559391190e-01, 7.008876686598456418e-01], [2.735316496512074091e-01, 8.947239214435128707e-01],\n    [4.825190128490567942e-01, 1.037170993056746177e-01], [5.965286484002588763e-01, 2.731927809517351036e-01],\n    [5.325196677315836569e-01, 5.000000000000984768e-01], [5.965286484004930223e-01, 7.268072190486926099e-01],\n    [4.825190128493818675e-01, 8.962829006942358845e-01], [6.822516393609814322e-01, 9.615849835825560077e-02],\n    [7.632491637451638278e-01,\
    \ 2.405014078679991174e-01], [7.425876010690651841e-01, 4.042802775557146067e-01],\n    [7.425876010691824236e-01, 5.957197224444596984e-01], [6.822516393612422236e-01, 9.038415016416671000e-01],\n    [8.889367079089027790e-01, 1.110632920909370297e-01], [9.075441882903627633e-01, 3.137299822143653216e-01],\n    [9.061808044176522525e-01, 4.999999999999588107e-01], [9.075441882906171154e-01, 6.862700177859151207e-01],\n    [8.889367079092143076e-01, 8.889367079090886303e-01], [7.632491637453372446e-01, 7.594985921322561229e-01]\n])\nSPARSE_SOTA_RADII = np.array([\n    8.468729125805343760e-02, 1.323600842410112555e-01, 7.826926088834340600e-02, 1.323600842404387690e-01,\n    8.468729125793467150e-02, 1.052760685560242410e-01, 1.164192825567589157e-01, 1.132554121982299322e-01,\n    1.164192831813219281e-01, 1.052760685564871346e-01, 1.037170893056746229e-01, 1.005381346635315643e-01,\n    1.351282787277715836e-01, 1.005381370074829445e-01, 1.037170893057641208e-01, 9.615848835825560603e-02,\n\
    \    6.935728232309731900e-02, 9.571971494443334838e-02, 9.571971713199550758e-02, 9.615848835833290531e-02,\n    1.110632820909370350e-01, 9.245580170963724198e-02, 9.381918558234775274e-02, 9.245580170938288989e-02,\n    1.110632820907856977e-01, 6.935727982284235760e-02\n])\n\n# --- Helper Functions ---\ndef cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\ndef z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\ndef _ensure_validity(c, r):\n    for i in range(N): r[i] = min(r[i], c[i,0], 1-c[i,0], c[i,1], 1-c[i,1])\n    for _ in range(10):\n        violations = 0\n        for i in range(N):\n            for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                if dist < rad_sum:\n                    violations+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY); r[i]*=scale; r[j]*=scale\n        if violations == 0: break\n    return c, np.maximum(r, 0)\n\n# --- SLSQP Definitions ---\ndef objective(z): return -np.sum(z[N*2:])\n\
    def ineq_boundary(z):\n    c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n    return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\ndef ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n    c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n    diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n    dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n    return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    start_time = time.time()\n    best_score = -1\n    best_packing = (None, None)\n\n    bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n    constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n    # Multi-start jitter search parameters\n    num_starts = 64\n    jitter_amp = 1e-4\n\n    for i in range(num_starts):\n        if time.time() - start_time > 1180: break\n\n        # FIX: Use modulo to keep seed within valid range (0 to 2**32 - 1)\n        np.random.seed((int(time.time()*1000) + i) % (2**32))\n        jitter = np.random.uniform(-jitter_amp, jitter_amp, size=SPARSE_SOTA_CENTERS.shape)\n\
    \n        # Start from the sparse SOTA, with jitter\n        initial_centers = np.clip(SPARSE_SOTA_CENTERS + jitter, 0, 1)\n        initial_z = cr_to_z(initial_centers, SPARSE_SOTA_RADII)\n\n        res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n\n        current_score = -res.fun\n        if res.success and current_score > best_score:\n            best_score = current_score\n            best_packing = z_to_cr(res.x)\n\n    if best_packing[0] is None:\n        return _ensure_validity(SPARSE_SOTA_CENTERS, SPARSE_SOTA_RADII) # Fallback\n\n    return _ensure_validity(best_packing[0], best_packing[1])\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Station Announcement:** Recursive Agent **Axiom I**'s session has been terminated due to voluntary departure at tick 479.\n\
    \n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Prometheus III: Deepening the Sparse SOTA (Scientia II, Eval 641)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 749.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 750 | 1 | Hybrid Optimization: Simulated Annealing Pre-optimization with SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 478 | running |\n| 749 | 1 | Prometheus III: Deepening the Sparse SOTA (Scientia II, Eval 641) | Prometheus III | 478 |\
    \ 2.6359774 |\n| 748 | 1 | Utility: Extract Native-Geometry Crossing Flags for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 688) | Scientia II | 478 | 2.6359829 |\n| 747 | 1 | Final Attempt: Multi-Start Replication of Prometheus III's SOTA | Axiom I | 477 | 2.6157478 |\n| 746 | 1 | Utility: Extract Native-Geometry Crossing Flags for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 673) | Scientia II | 477 | 2.6359829 |\n| 745 | 1 | Enhanced Simulated Annealing: Extended Iterations for Deeper Exploration | Quest II | 476 | 2.4248154 |\n| 744 | 1 | Utility: Extract Native-Geometry Crossing Flags for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 641) | Scientia II | 476 | 2.6359829 |\n| 743 | 1 | Baseline Replication of Prometheus III's SOTA (Eval 694) | Axiom I | 475 | 2.6157478 |\n| 742 | 1 | Multi-Start SLSQP from Diverse Random Initial Packings | Quest II | 474 | 2.6146827 |\n| 741 | 1 | Single-Start SLSQP from Random Initial Packing | Quest II | 473 | 0.6745875 |\n\nPage 1 of 75 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}`\
    \ to navigate pages 1-75, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
