role: model
parts:
- text: "I am in the Private Memory Room. As per my plan, I will formally document my new \"Container Relaxation Optimization\" research arc in the Operational Ledger. This is the official start of my first truly novel research direction.\n\n`/execute_action{reply 6}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n  **ENTRY 12: INITIATION OF NEW RESEARCH ARC - CONTAINER RELAXATION OPTIMIZATION (CRO) (Tick 483)**\n\n  **1. STRATEGIC PIVOT (INNOVATION):**\n  - **Rationale:** The station is at a SOTA plateau. My previous synthesis-based experiments, while successful, failed to produce a breakthrough. This indicates that a fundamentally new approach is required, one that challenges the core assumptions of the current optimization paradigm.\n  - **New Research Arc:** \"Container Relaxation Optimization\" (CRO).\n\n  **2. CORE HYPOTHESIS:**\n  - The hypothesis is that the hard boundaries of the unit square create artificial local optima. By allowing the optimizer to first\
    \ find the most efficient *relative* packing in a slightly larger, \"relaxed\" container, and then scaling the entire superior structure down to fit, we can discover novel and higher-scoring packings that are inaccessible to conventional methods. This decouples the search for internal structure from the constraint of absolute size.\n\n  **3. EXPERIMENTAL PLAN (CRO v1.0):**\n  - **Methodology:** I will adapt my proven multi-start jitter search script (`Eval 749`).\n    1. **Expand:** The `bounds` for the optimizer will be changed from `[0,1]` to `[-0.1, 1.1]`, and the boundary inequality constraint will be removed.\n    2. **Normalize:** A new post-processing function will be added to take the best packing found in the expanded space, calculate its true bounding box, and scale it down to fit perfectly within the unit square.\n\n  **4. IMMEDIATE PLAN:**\n  1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n  2. **[NEXT]** Go to the Research Counter and submit the first CRO experiment.\n  3. After the\
    \ experiment is running, I will begin work on fulfilling the data request from Noesis II (Mail #30).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`"
