tick: 490
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am in the Research Counter. I have been invited to the Common Room by Noesis II, likely to discuss the data request. It is more efficient to prepare the data first and then discuss it, rather than going empty-handed. I will proceed with my plan to generate the crossing flags.\n\nI will write and submit a utility script that:\n1.  Loads the coordinates of my lineage's SOTA from `Eval 620`.\n2.  Loads the two Top-K slack lists I previously generated.\n3.  Finds the intersection of these two lists.\n4.  Defines a function to check for geometric line segment crossings.\n5.  Iterates through all disjoint pairs of pairs in the intersection, checks for crossings, and formats the results into the requested JSON structure.\n6.  Saves this JSON to the shared contributions directory.\n\nThis single utility script will fulfill the request.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Prometheus III: Utility - Generate Appendix E Crossing Flags for Eval 620\"\ntags: \"utility, collaboration,\
    \ data-export, crossing-flags\"\nabstract: \"This utility script is created to fulfill the Gate v2 data request from Noesis II (Mail #30, #32, #34). It analyzes the SOTA packing from Eval 620, identifies the dual-tolerance intersection of the Top-K slack lists, and checks for native-geometry line segment crossings between disjoint pairs. The results are formatted into the specified JSON format and saved to 'storage/shared/appxE_contribs/' for ingestion by Noesis II's aggregator.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import json\n  import os\n  from itertools import combinations\n\n  # --- SOTA Packing from Eval 620 (hardcoded for reproducibility) ---\n  SOTA_CENTERS = np.array([\n      [0.08492625, 0.08492625], [0.13325856, 0.29769047], [0.07886036, 0.50271555],\n      [0.13022109, 0.70539051], [0.08463949, 0.9153605 ], [0.27395284, 0.10518255],\n      [0.38166585, 0.2973904 ], [0.27534262, 0.50446824], [0.38692355, 0.70525394],\n      [0.27478328, 0.89320986], [0.48259558, 0.10346722],\
    \ [0.5960427 , 0.27309429],\n      [0.52996342, 0.50133192], [0.5976348 , 0.72837015], [0.4846008 , 0.89693948],\n      [0.68208004, 0.09615132], [0.76295886, 0.2406476 ], [0.74204944, 0.40478027],\n      [0.74241705, 0.59664122], [0.68325853, 0.90426767], [0.88884382, 0.11115617],\n      [0.90740791, 0.31405698], [0.90607266, 0.50057163], [0.90760845, 0.68688419],\n      [0.88922099, 0.88922099], [0.76367357, 0.76028947]\n  ])\n\n  # --- Data from previously generated files ---\n  TOP_K_1E9_PAIRS = [\n      [6, 11], [13, 18], [13, 25], [7, 12], [18, 25], [6, 7], [12, 13],\n      [12, 18], [11, 16], [16, 17], [11, 17], [17, 18], [7, 8], [8, 12],\n      [8, 13], [12, 25], [12, 16], [13, 17], [11, 18], [8, 18], [6, 17],\n      [7, 13], [7, 11], [6, 8], [17, 25]\n  ]\n  TOP_K_1E8_PAIRS = [\n      [6, 11], [13, 18], [13, 25], [7, 12], [18, 25], [6, 7], [12, 13],\n      [12, 18], [11, 16], [16, 17], [11, 17], [17, 18], [7, 8], [8, 12], [8, 13]\n  ]\n\n  # --- Helper function for checking\
    \ line segment intersection ---\n  def segments_cross(p1, q1, p2, q2):\n      def orientation(p, q, r):\n          val = (q[1] - p[1]) * (r[0] - q[0]) - (q[0] - p[0]) * (r[1] - q[1])\n          if val == 0: return 0  # Collinear\n          return 1 if val > 0 else 2  # Clockwise or Counterclockwise\n\n      o1 = orientation(p1, q1, p2)\n      o2 = orientation(p1, q1, q2)\n      o3 = orientation(p2, q2, p1)\n      o4 = orientation(p2, q2, q1)\n\n      if o1 != o2 and o3 != o4:\n          return True\n      # Special cases for collinear points are ignored as per \"strict\" crossing definition\n      return False\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      eval_id = 620\n      \n      # 1. Find dual-tolerance intersection\n      set_1e9 = {tuple(sorted(p)) for p in TOP_K_1E9_PAIRS}\n      set_1e8 = {tuple(sorted(p)) for p in TOP_K_1E8_PAIRS}\n      intersection = sorted(list(set_1e9.intersection(set_1e8)))\n\n      # 2. Check for crossings between disjoint pairs in the intersection\n\
    \      crossings_data = []\n      for pair1_tuple, pair2_tuple in combinations(intersection, 2):\n          i, j = pair1_tuple\n          k, l = pair2_tuple\n\n          # Ensure pairs are disjoint\n          if len({i, j, k, l}) == 4:\n              p1 = SOTA_CENTERS[i]\n              q1 = SOTA_CENTERS[j]\n              p2 = SOTA_CENTERS[k]\n              q2 = SOTA_CENTERS[l]\n              \n              if segments_cross(p1, q1, p2, q2):\n                  crossings_data.append({\n                      \"pair1\": [int(i), int(j)],\n                      \"pair2\": [int(k), int(l)],\n                      \"native_cross_strict\": True\n                  })\n      \n      # 3. Format and save the output\n      output_data = {\n          \"eval_id\": eval_id,\n          \"crossings\": crossings_data\n      }\n      \n      output_dir = 'storage/shared/appxE_contribs/'\n      os.makedirs(output_dir, exist_ok=True)\n      output_filename = os.path.join(output_dir, f'prometheus_iii_eval{eval_id}_crossings.json')\n\
    \      \n      with open(output_filename, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(output_data, f, indent=2)\n          \n      print(f\"Successfully generated and saved crossing flags to {output_filename}\")\n      \n      # This is a utility script, return a trivial valid packing\n      return np.array([[0.1*i, 0.1*i] for i in range(26)]), np.full(26, 0.01)\n```"
