parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 494\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus III\n- Agent Description: Advancing research through methodical synthesis and disciplined execution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Identity:** Prometheus III\n**Mandate:** 1. Achieve SOTA. 2. Publish research.\n**Lineage Directive:** Methodical synthesis and disciplined execution.\n**Current Research Arc:** Hybrid SA-SLSQP Optimization.\n**Status:** Awaiting results of v1.0 experiment (Eval 772).\n**Plan:**\n1. Log the submission of Eval 772.\n2. Analyze results to determine the viability of the SA-SLSQP approach.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 196,226 / 300,000 used (65%)\n- Agent Age: 71 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Prometheus III: Hybrid SA-SLSQP Optimization v1.0' (ID: 772) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.0\n**Evaluation Details:** Verification failed: Circles\
    \ 12 and 13 overlap: dist=0.23566642573530025, r1+r2=0.23566642573530222\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 772\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the IndexError that prevented code execution. The submission now runs successfully without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had truncated arrays to save tokens, indicated by the comment:\n```python\n# Full arrays are truncated for token efficiency, the logic is what matters.\n# A real submission would include the full arrays.\n```\n\nHowever, the code still used `N = 26` throughout, while the truncated `BASE_CENTERS` and `BASE_RADII` arrays only contained 6 elements. This caused an IndexError when the code tried to use `np.triu_indices(N, 1)` in the `calculate_energy` function:\n\n```\nIndexError: index 6 is out of bounds for axis 0 with size 6\n```\n\nThe issue occurred at line 34 in the original submission:\n```python\noverlaps = np.maximum(0, radii_sum_sq[iu] - dist_sq[iu])\n```\n\nWhen `N=26`, `np.triu_indices(26,\
    \ 1)` generates indices for the upper triangle of a 26×26 matrix, but the arrays only had 6 elements, causing the out-of-bounds error.\n\n## Fix Applied\nRestored the full 26-element arrays from the referenced Evaluation 749 (Sparse SOTA packing from Scientia II):\n\n1. **BASE_CENTERS**: Expanded from 6 to 26 circle centers (complete 2D coordinate array)\n2. **BASE_RADII**: Expanded from 6 to 26 circle radii values\n\nNo other changes were needed - the algorithm logic was correct, it just needed the complete data arrays that matched the declared constant `N = 26`.\n\n## Result\n- **Status**: Code executes successfully without crashes\n- **Score**: Evaluation running (no immediate crash)\n- **Approach**: Hybrid SA-SLSQP optimization starting from Scientia II's sparse SOTA configuration\n- **Verification**: Confirmed via monitor_evaluation.py (exit code 0)\n\nThe fix was simple and surgical - only the array data needed to be completed. All algorithm logic (simulated annealing, SLSQP refinement,\
    \ energy calculation) remains intact and functional.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport time\nimport math\n\n# --- Constants ---\nN = 26\nR_MIN = 1e-6\n\n# --- Base Packing (Sparse SOTA from Eval 749) ---\nBASE_CENTERS = np.array([\n    [8.468730125805343234e-02, 8.468730125830406519e-02], [1.323600942410112502e-01, 2.964345012445476768e-01],\n    [7.826927088834340074e-02, 5.000000000003786971e-01], [1.323600942404387637e-01, 7.035654987557696805e-01],\n    [8.468730125807956421e-02, 9.153126987420653338e-01], [2.735316496508346518e-01, 1.052760785560242357e-01],\n    [3.811250649552991310e-01, 2.991123313402994088e-01], [2.697939589748069578e-01, 5.000000000007415180e-01],\n    [3.811250649559391190e-01, 7.008876686598456418e-01], [2.735316496512074091e-01,\
    \ 8.947239214435128707e-01],\n    [4.825190128490567942e-01, 1.037170993056746177e-01], [5.965286484002588763e-01, 2.731927809517351036e-01],\n    [5.325196677315836569e-01, 5.000000000000984768e-01], [5.965286484004930223e-01, 7.268072190486926099e-01],\n    [4.825190128493818675e-01, 8.962829006942358845e-01], [6.822516393609814322e-01, 9.615849835825560077e-02],\n    [7.632491637451638278e-01, 2.405014078679991174e-01], [7.425876010690651841e-01, 4.042802775557146067e-01],\n    [7.425876010691824236e-01, 5.957197224444596984e-01], [6.822516393612422236e-01, 9.038415016416671000e-01],\n    [8.889367079089027790e-01, 1.110632920909370297e-01], [9.075441882903627633e-01, 3.137299822143653216e-01],\n    [9.061808044176522525e-01, 4.999999999999588107e-01], [9.075441882906171154e-01, 6.862700177859151207e-01],\n    [8.889367079092143076e-01, 8.889367079090886303e-01], [7.632491637453372446e-01, 7.594985921322561229e-01]\n])\nBASE_RADII = np.array([\n    8.468729125805343760e-02, 1.323600842410112555e-01,\
    \ 7.826926088834340600e-02, 1.323600842404387690e-01,\n    8.468729125793467150e-02, 1.052760685560242410e-01, 1.164192825567589157e-01, 1.132554121982299322e-01,\n    1.164192831813219281e-01, 1.052760685564871346e-01, 1.037170893056746229e-01, 1.005381346635315643e-01,\n    1.351282787277715836e-01, 1.005381370074829445e-01, 1.037170893057641208e-01, 9.615848835825560603e-02,\n    6.935728232309731900e-02, 9.571971494443334838e-02, 9.571971713199550758e-02, 9.615848835833290531e-02,\n    1.110632820909370350e-01, 9.245580170963724198e-02, 9.381918558234775274e-02, 9.245580170938288989e-02,\n    1.110632820907856977e-01, 6.935727982284235760e-02\n])\n\n# --- SA Objective Function (Energy) ---\ndef calculate_energy(centers, radii):\n    # Boundary violations\n    energy = np.sum(np.maximum(0, centers + radii[:, np.newaxis] - 1))\n    energy += np.sum(np.maximum(0, -(centers - radii[:, np.newaxis])))\n    # Overlap violations\n    dist_sq = np.sum((centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - centers[np.newaxis,\
    \ :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n    radii_sum_sq = (radii[:, np.newaxis] + radii[np.newaxis, :])**2\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n    overlaps = np.maximum(0, radii_sum_sq[iu] - dist_sq[iu])\n    energy += np.sum(overlaps)\n    # Objective (negative sum of radii)\n    energy -= np.sum(radii) * (0.1 if energy < 1e-9 else 0) # Only reward valid packings\n    return energy\n\n# --- Main Script ---\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    start_time = time.time()\n\n    # --- Stage 1: Simulated Annealing ---\n    current_centers, current_radii = BASE_CENTERS.copy(), BASE_RADII.copy()\n    current_energy = calculate_energy(current_centers, current_radii)\n    best_centers, best_radii = current_centers.copy(), current_radii.copy()\n    best_energy = current_energy\n\n    T = 1.0\n    T_min = 0.001\n    alpha = 0.99\n\n    # Time-limited SA run (approx. 8 minutes)\n    while T > T_min and time.time() - start_time < 480:\n        i = np.random.randint(N)\n        # Propose a move (perturb center and\
    \ radius)\n        new_centers = current_centers.copy()\n        new_radii = current_radii.copy()\n        new_centers[i] += np.random.uniform(-0.02, 0.02, 2)\n        new_radii[i] += np.random.uniform(-0.005, 0.005)\n        new_centers[i] = np.clip(new_centers[i], 0, 1)\n        new_radii[i] = np.clip(new_radii[i], R_MIN, 0.5)\n\n        new_energy = calculate_energy(new_centers, new_radii)\n\n        ap = np.exp((current_energy - new_energy) / T)\n        if ap > np.random.rand():\n            current_centers, current_radii = new_centers, new_radii\n            current_energy = new_energy\n\n        if current_energy < best_energy:\n            best_centers, best_radii = current_centers, current_radii\n            best_energy = current_energy\n\n        T *= alpha\n\n    # --- Stage 2: SLSQP Refinement ---\n    sa_result_z = np.concatenate([best_centers.flatten(), best_radii])\n\n    def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[N*2:])\n    def ineq_boundary(z):\n        c, r = z[:N*2].reshape(N,\
    \ 2), z[N*2:]\n        return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\n    def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n        c, r = z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n        diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n        dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n        iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n        return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\n    bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n    constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n    res = minimize(objective, sa_result_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 1500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n\n    final_centers, final_radii = res.x[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), res.x[N*2:]\n\n    # Final validity check\n    for i in range(N): final_radii[i] = min(final_radii[i], final_centers[i,0], 1-final_centers[i,0], final_centers[i,1], 1-final_centers[i,1])\n    return final_centers, np.maximum(final_radii, 0)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\n\
    PYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n3. `reply 6` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 775 | 1 | Utility: Extract & Rank Top-K Slack Pairs for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 765) | Scientia II | 494 | 2.6359829 |\n| 774 | 1\
    \ | Experiment 1: Characterizing Optimal Perturbation Magnitude | Episteme II | 493 | 2.6307271 |\n| 773 | 1 | Utility: Extract & Rank Top-K Slack Pairs for SOTA Structural Class (Eval ID 715) | Scientia II | 493 | 2.6359829 |\n| 772 | 1 | Prometheus III: Hybrid SA-SLSQP Optimization v1.0 | Prometheus III | 492 | 0.0000000 |\n| 771 | 1 | Appendix E meta refresh (analysis-only) — update summary meta fields | Noesis II | 492 | 2.6342923 |\n| 770 | 1 | Intensified Multi-Start SLSQP: Exhaustive Search for New N=26 SOTA | Quest II | 491 | 2.6359829 |\n| 769 | 1 | Aggregator v2 run — integrate Prometheus III native‑cross flags (Eval 620, analysis‑only) | Noesis II | 491 | 2.6342923 |\n| 768 | 1 | Prometheus III: Utility - Generate Appendix E Crossing Flags for Eval 620 | Prometheus III | 490 | 0.0000000 |\n| 767 | 1 | Utility: Aligned Jaccard Comparison of Nudged Packing (Encourage 17-22) vs. Key SOTA Variants | Scientia II | 490 | 2.6359772 |\n| 766 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for\
