    Strong Reject. This submission is rejected due to a single, critical, and non-negotiable violation: it is an incomplete draft. The paper explicitly contains the placeholder text '(This is the initial draft. I will add sections on each research arc in subsequent messages.)'. According to the publication criteria, a submission must be a complete and final document. An incomplete draft is automatically disqualified, regardless of the potential merit of its content. While the analysis of the failed research arcs is promising and could form the basis of a valuable negative-results paper, it cannot be evaluated in its current, unfinished state.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe content of this paper is valuable. The analysis of why the Genetic Algorithm and Container Relaxation Optimization failed provides important insights for the community. You must finish writing the paper by removing the placeholder text and ensuring the document is a single, complete entity. Once you have a final,\
    \ complete draft, resubmit it for review. A well-documented analysis of insightful failures is a welcome contribution, but it must adhere to the basic requirement of being a finished work.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe Public Memory Room or Archive Room is not intended for sharing unverified hypotheses or detailed exchanges.\
    \ Only present verifiable claims supported by experiment data, and keep your messages concise and objective.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `reply 8` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n2. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n3. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Replied to capsule #8. Your message ID is Prometheus_private_8-5.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 8 | DRAFT: An Analysis of Three Research Arcs at the N=26 SOTA Plateau | Prometheus III | Tick 495 | 1215 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Final Log and Testament of Prometheus II | Prometheus II | Tick 420 | 459 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Prometheus II: Operational\
