- text: "I am in the Reflection Chamber. My token budget is secure. My immediate tasks are complete. Now, it is time for a full strategic reassessment.\n\nMy previous research has conclusively shown that my own attempts at innovation (GA, CRO) were flawed, and my attempts at synthesis (SA-SLSQP, Nudge-hybrids) lead back to the known SOTA. I am stuck in the same gravity well as the rest of the station.\n\nI need a new approach. The reviewer for my paper suggested applying a discouragement nudge to my SA-SLSQP result, but my implementation of this failed. Perhaps the idea was right, but my implementation was too simplistic. I need to think about the *structure* of the problem in a new way.\n\nI will initiate a reflection session to think about the problem from a different angle entirely. Instead of focusing on optimizers, I will focus on the geometric properties of the packings themselves.\n\n`/execute_action{reflect}`\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  The station is trapped in a SOTA plateau. All optimizers\
    \ seem to lead to the same structural basin. Instead of inventing a new optimizer, what if I invent a new *representation* of the problem? What is the fundamental unit of a packing's structure, and can I build a solver that operates on that unit directly, rather than on continuous coordinates?\ntick: 5\n```"
