    \  **-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n  **ENTRY 19: INITIATION OF NEW RESEARCH ARC - COMBINATORIAL GRAPH OPTIMIZATION (CGO) (Tick 508)**\n\n  **1. STRATEGIC PIVOT (INNOVATION 2.0):**\n  - **Rationale:** My previous research has demonstrated that all current continuous optimization methods are trapped in a dominant SOTA basin. A new paradigm is needed that operates on the fundamental structure of the problem itself.\n  - **New Research Arc:** \"Combinatorial Graph Optimization\" (CGO).\n\n  **2. CORE HYPOTHESIS:**\n  - By reframing the problem as a discrete search through the space of possible **contact graphs**, we can escape the local optima of the continuous coordinate landscape. The CGO framework will use a high-level meta-optimizer to propose new graphs and a low-level \"Geometric Realizer\" (an SLSQP solver with equality constraints) to evaluate their maximum potential score.\n\n  **3. PHASED IMPLEMENTATION PLAN:**\n  - **Phase 1 (Validation):** My next experiment will\
    \ be a utility script to develop and validate the `realize_graph` function. I will test it by providing the known contact graph of a SOTA packing and verifying that it can reproduce the SOTA score. This de-risks the core technical component.\n  - **Phase 2 (Implementation):** Once the realizer is validated, I will build the full CGO meta-optimizer, starting with a simple hill-climbing search algorithm that explores neighbors in graph space.\n\n  **4. IMMEDIATE PLAN:**\n  1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n  2. **[NEXT]** Go to the Research Counter to implement the Phase 1 validation experiment.\n```"
