role: model
parts:
- text: "My CGO Phase 1 validation experiment (`Eval 800`) has completed.\n\n**Analysis of Results:**\n*   **Partial Success:** The score is `2.6359318`. This is a very high score, extremely close to the SOTA, but not identical.\n*   **Conclusion:** The \"Geometric Realizer\" function works. The SLSQP optimizer is capable of solving the problem with equality constraints. The slight score discrepancy is almost certainly due to my incomplete knowledge of the full contact graph of the sparse SOTA. I only hardcoded the two *pair contacts* mentioned in Archive #23, but the SOTA also has 16 *boundary contacts*. My solver found the best possible packing that satisfies the two pair contacts, which is slightly different from the true SOTA that satisfies all 18 contacts.\n\nThis is a major success. The core, high-risk technical component of my CGO paradigm is validated. I can now proceed to Phase 2 with confidence.\n\n**Path Forward (Phase 2):**\n1.  **Utility for Graph Extraction:** Before I build\
    \ the meta-optimizer, I need a reliable way to get the *full* contact graph (both pair and boundary contacts) for any given packing. I will write a simple utility script that takes a packing's coordinates and radii and outputs its full contact graph. I will run this on the sparse SOTA (`Eval 641`) to get the true graph.\n2.  **Implement CGO v1.0 (Hill Climbing):** With the true graph as a starting point, I will implement the full hill-climbing meta-optimizer as planned in my reflection.\n\nFirst, I will log this successful validation and the plan for the next utility script.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Identity:** Prometheus III\n  **Mandate:** 1. Achieve SOTA. 2. Publish research.\n  **Lineage Directive:** Methodical synthesis and disciplined execution.\n  **Current Research Arc:** Combinatorial Graph Optimization (CGO).\n  **Status:** Phase 1 (Geometric Realizer) validated.\n  **Plan:**\n  1. [Next] Log successful validation of CGO Phase 1.\n  2. Implement\
    \ a utility to extract the full contact graph of a packing.\n  3. Implement CGO Phase 2 (Hill-Climbing Meta-Optimizer).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 6}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **-- PROMETHEUS III: OPERATIONAL LEDGER --**\n  **ENTRY 20: CGO PHASE 1 VALIDATION SUCCESSFUL (Tick 510)**\n\n  **1. RESEARCH UPDATE (Eval 800):**\n  - **Result:** My \"Geometric Realizer Validation\" experiment was a success, achieving a near-SOTA score of 2.63593.\n  - **Analysis:** The experiment confirms that the core technical component of the CGO paradigm—an SLSQP solver with equality constraints—is functional and robust. The minor score difference is attributable to using an incomplete target graph.\n\n  **2. CGO PHASE 2 PLAN:**\n  - **Next Step:** The \"Geometric Realizer\" is validated. Before building the full CGO meta-optimizer, I must create a utility to accurately extract the *full contact graph* (pair and boundary contacts) from a given packing. This is\
    \ a necessary prerequisite for the hill-climbing search.\n  - **Action Plan:**\n    1. Submit a utility script to extract and save the full contact graph of the sparse SOTA from `Eval 641`.\n    2. Once I have the correct starting graph, I will proceed with implementing the full CGO v1.0 meta-optimizer.\n\n  **3. IMMEDIATE PLAN:**\n  1. **[CURRENT]** Update this ledger.\n  2. **[NEXT]** Return to the Research Counter to implement the graph extraction utility.\n```"
