tick: 511
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have updated my ledger. My next step is to create the graph extraction utility. This will be a simple script that loads the packing data from the sparse SOTA (`Eval 641`), calculates all active contacts (pair and boundary), and saves them to a file in my lineage's storage for future use.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Prometheus III: CGO Utility - Full Contact Graph Extractor\"\ntags: \"cgo, utility, data-extraction, contact-graph\"\nabstract: \"This utility script is a prerequisite for my CGO Phase 2 experiment. It loads a target packing (the sparse SOTA from Eval 641), identifies all active pair contacts and boundary contacts within a given tolerance, and saves this complete contact graph to a JSON file in my lineage's storage. This provides a reliable, machine-readable starting point for the CGO meta-optimizer's search in graph space.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\n\
    \  import json\n  import os\n\n  # --- Constants ---\n  N = 26\n  TOLERANCE = 1e-6\n\n  # --- Target Packing (Sparse SOTA from Eval 641) ---\n  CENTERS = np.array([\n      [8.4687301258e-02, 8.4687301258e-02], [1.3236009424e-01, 2.9643450124e-01],\n      [7.8269270888e-02, 5.0000000000e-01], [1.3236009424e-01, 7.0356549876e-01],\n      [8.4687301258e-02, 9.1531269874e-01], [2.7353164965e-01, 1.0527607856e-01],\n      [3.8112506496e-01, 2.9911233134e-01], [2.6979395897e-01, 5.0000000000e-01],\n      [3.8112506496e-01, 7.0088766866e-01], [2.7353164965e-01, 8.9472392144e-01],\n      [4.8251901285e-01, 1.0371709931e-01], [5.9652864840e-01, 2.7319278095e-01],\n      [5.3251966773e-01, 5.0000000000e-01], [5.9652864840e-01, 7.2680721905e-01],\n      [4.8251901285e-01, 8.9628290069e-01], [6.8225163936e-01, 9.6158498358e-02],\n      [7.6324916375e-01, 2.4050140787e-01], [7.4258760107e-01, 4.0428027756e-01],\n      [7.4258760107e-01, 5.9571972244e-01], [6.8225163936e-01, 9.0384150164e-01],\n \
    \     [8.8893670791e-01, 1.1106329209e-01], [9.0754418829e-01, 3.1372998221e-01],\n      [9.0618080442e-01, 5.0000000000e-01], [9.0754418829e-01, 6.8627001779e-01],\n      [8.8893670791e-01, 8.8893670791e-01], [7.6324916375e-01, 7.5949859213e-01]\n  ])\n  RADII = np.array([\n      8.4687291258e-02, 1.3236008424e-01, 7.8269260888e-02, 1.3236008424e-01,\n      8.4687291258e-02, 1.0527606856e-01, 1.1641928256e-01, 1.1325541220e-01,\n      1.1641928318e-01, 1.0527606856e-01, 1.0371708931e-01, 1.0053813466e-01,\n      1.3512827873e-01, 1.0053813701e-01, 1.0371708931e-01, 9.6158488358e-02,\n      6.9357282323e-02, 9.5719714944e-02, 9.5719717132e-02, 9.6158488358e-02,\n      1.1106328209e-01, 9.2455801710e-02, 9.3819185582e-02, 9.2455801709e-02,\n      1.1106328209e-01, 6.9357279823e-02\n  ])\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      # --- Extract Pair Contacts ---\n      pair_contacts = []\n      dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(CENTERS))\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i\
    \ + 1, N):\n              if abs(dist_matrix[i, j] - (RADII[i] + RADII[j])) < TOLERANCE:\n                  pair_contacts.append([i, j])\n\n      # --- Extract Boundary Contacts ---\n      boundary_contacts = []\n      for i in range(N):\n          if abs(CENTERS[i, 0] - RADII[i]) < TOLERANCE:\n              boundary_contacts.append([i, \"xL\"])\n          if abs(1 - (CENTERS[i, 0] + RADII[i])) < TOLERANCE:\n              boundary_contacts.append([i, \"xR\"])\n          if abs(CENTERS[i, 1] - RADII[i]) < TOLERANCE:\n              boundary_contacts.append([i, \"yB\"])\n          if abs(1 - (CENTERS[i, 1] + RADII[i])) < TOLERANCE:\n              boundary_contacts.append([i, \"yT\"])\n\n      # --- Save to Lineage Storage ---\n      output_data = {\n          \"eval_id\": 641,\n          \"pair_contacts\": sorted(pair_contacts),\n          \"boundary_contacts\": sorted(boundary_contacts)\n      }\n      \n      output_dir = 'storage/prometheus/cgo_data/'\n      os.makedirs(output_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\
    \      output_filename = os.path.join(output_dir, f'eval_641_full_graph.json')\n      \n      with open(output_filename, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(output_data, f, indent=2)\n          \n      print(f\"Successfully extracted and saved contact graph to {output_filename}\")\n      \n      # Return the original packing, as this is a utility\n      return CENTERS, RADII\n```"
