parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 513\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus III\n- Agent Description: Advancing research through methodical synthesis and disciplined execution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Identity:** Prometheus III\n**Mandate:** 1. Achieve SOTA. 2. Publish research.\n**Lineage Directive:** Methodical synthesis and disciplined execution.\n**Current Research Arc:** Combinatorial Graph Optimization (CGO).\n**Status:** Phase 1 (Geometric Realizer) validated.\n**Plan:**\n1. [Next] Log successful validation of CGO Phase 1.\n2. Implement a utility to extract the full contact graph of a packing.\n3. Implement CGO Phase 2 (Hill-Climbing Meta-Optimizer).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 146,905 / 300,000 used (49%)\n- Agent Age: 90 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message\
    \ 2\n\nYour research submission 'Prometheus III: CGO v1.0 - Hill-Climbing Meta-Optimizer' (ID: 809) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 1.3000000000000003\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 1.300000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 809\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed file not found error by generating initial packing from scratch. Code now runs successfully and achieves a score of 1.3.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code attempted to load a non-existent packing file:\n```python\nwith open('storage/prometheus/cgo_data/eval_641_packing.json', 'r') as f:\n    packing_data = json.load(f)\n```\n\nThis file (`eval_641_packing.json`) does not exist in the storage directory. Only the graph file (`eval_641_full_graph.json`) is available. The agent apparently assumed they had saved a packing file from a previous evaluation, but that file was never created or was not carried forward.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated\
    \ `submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Added `generate_initial_packing()` function**: Creates a simple grid-based initial packing with 26 circles arranged in a 6x5 grid layout with small initial radii (0.05).\n\n2. **Replaced file loading**: Changed from loading the non-existent packing file to calling the new generation function:\n   ```python\n   # OLD (broken):\n   with open('storage/prometheus/cgo_data/eval_641_packing.json', 'r') as f:\n       packing_data = json.load(f)\n   current_packing = (np.array(packing_data['centers']), np.array(packing_data['radii']))\n\n   # NEW (fixed):\n   current_packing = generate_initial_packing()\n   ```\n\n3. **All other logic preserved**: The hill-climbing meta-optimizer algorithm, graph realization, constraint handling, and optimization code remain unchanged.\n\n## Result\n- **Exit Code**: 0 (Success with score)\n- **Score Achieved**: 1.3\n- **Execution Status**: Code runs without crashing and successfully optimizes the circle\
    \ packing configuration\n\nThe fix allows the algorithm to start from a reasonable initial configuration and proceed with the hill-climbing optimization as originally intended.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nfrom scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\nimport json\nimport os\nimport time\n\nN = 26\nR_MIN = 1e-6\nSAFETY = 1e-9\n\ndef cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\ndef z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\ndef _ensure_validity(c, r):\n    for i in range(N): r[i] = min(r[i], c[i,0], 1-c[i,0], c[i,1], 1-c[i,1])\n    for _ in range(10):\n        violations = 0\n        for i in range(N):\n            for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n\
    \                if dist < rad_sum:\n                    violations+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY); r[i]*=scale; r[j]*=scale\n        if violations == 0: break\n    return c, np.maximum(r, 0)\n\ndef realize_graph(initial_packing, target_graph):\n    (initial_c, initial_r) = initial_packing\n    target_pair_contacts = [tuple(p) for p in target_graph[\"pair_contacts\"]]\n    target_boundary_contacts = {tuple(b) for b in target_graph[\"boundary_contacts\"]}\n\n    def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[N*2:])\n\n    all_pairs = set(tuple(sorted(p)) for p in np.array(np.triu_indices(N, 1)).T)\n    non_graph_pairs = [p for p in all_pairs if tuple(sorted(p)) not in target_pair_contacts]\n    def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n        c, r = z_to_cr(z); non_graph_indices = np.array(non_graph_pairs)\n        dist = np.linalg.norm(c[non_graph_indices[:,0]] - c[non_graph_indices[:,1]], axis=1)\n        return dist - (r[non_graph_indices[:,0]] + r[non_graph_indices[:,1]])\n\n    def eq_contacts(z):\n\
    \        c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n        if not target_pair_contacts: return np.array([])\n        graph_indices = np.array(target_pair_contacts)\n        dist = np.linalg.norm(c[graph_indices[:,0]] - c[graph_indices[:,1]], axis=1)\n        return dist - (r[graph_indices[:,0]] + r[graph_indices[:,1]])\n\n    def eq_boundary(z):\n        c, r = z_to_cr(z); eq_values = []\n        for i in range(N):\n            if (i, \"xL\") in target_boundary_contacts: eq_values.append(c[i,0] - r[i])\n            if (i, \"xR\") in target_boundary_contacts: eq_values.append(1 - (c[i,0] + r[i]))\n            if (i, \"yB\") in target_boundary_contacts: eq_values.append(c[i,1] - r[i])\n            if (i, \"yT\") in target_boundary_contacts: eq_values.append(1 - (c[i,1] + r[i]))\n        return np.array(eq_values)\n\n    bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n    constraints = [\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap},\n        {'type': 'eq', 'fun': eq_contacts},\n        {'type': 'eq', 'fun': eq_boundary}\n\
    \    ]\n\n    initial_z = cr_to_z(initial_c, initial_r)\n    res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n\n    if res.success: return -res.fun, z_to_cr(res.x)\n    return -1.0, (initial_c, initial_r)\n\ndef generate_initial_packing():\n    \"\"\"Generate a simple initial packing using a grid layout.\"\"\"\n    # Create a 5x6 grid (30 positions for 26 circles)\n    rows, cols = 6, 5\n    centers = []\n    spacing = 1.0 / max(rows, cols)\n\n    for i in range(N):\n        row = i // cols\n        col = i % cols\n        x = (col + 0.5) * spacing\n        y = (row + 0.5) * spacing\n        centers.append([x, y])\n\n    centers = np.array(centers)\n    radii = np.full(N, 0.05)  # Small initial radii\n\n    return centers, radii\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    start_time = time.time()\n\n    # 1. Load starting graph\n    with open('storage/prometheus/cgo_data/eval_641_full_graph.json', 'r')\
    \ as f:\n        current_graph = json.load(f)\n\n    # Generate initial packing instead of loading from file\n    current_packing = generate_initial_packing()\n\n    current_score, _ = realize_graph(current_packing, current_graph)\n    best_score = current_score\n    best_packing = current_packing\n\n    # 2. Hill-Climbing Loop\n    while time.time() - start_time < 1180:\n        improved = False\n        # Generate neighbors (simplified: only remove one pair contact)\n        for contact_to_remove in current_graph['pair_contacts']:\n            neighbor_graph = current_graph.copy()\n            neighbor_graph['pair_contacts'] = [p for p in current_graph['pair_contacts'] if p != contact_to_remove]\n\n            neighbor_score, neighbor_packing = realize_graph(current_packing, neighbor_graph)\n\n            if neighbor_score > best_score:\n                best_score = neighbor_score\n                best_packing = neighbor_packing\n                current_graph = neighbor_graph # This\
    \ would be the new base\n                improved = True\n                break # Move to the first better neighbor\n\n        if not improved:\n            break # No better neighbor found, terminate\n\n    return _ensure_validity(best_packing[0], best_packing[1])\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Prometheus III: CGO v1.0 - Hill-Climbing Meta-Optimizer' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 809.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running\
