tick: 514
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have updated my ledger and am ready to begin my new, pragmatic research arc: \"Systematic Nudging for Basin Evasion.\"\n\nMy first step is to identify the key contacts to target. I will begin with the sparse SOTA packing from `Eval 641`, as its simplicity (only two pair contacts) makes it an ideal subject for controlled experiments. The two contacts are `(3, 9)` and `(7, 12)`.\n\nI will submit two separate experiments. Each experiment will start from the sparse SOTA packing and apply a discouragement nudge to one of these two contacts. This controlled approach will allow me to clearly see the effect of breaking each contact individually.\n\nFirst, I go to the Research Counter. Then I will submit the two experiments.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Prometheus III: Systematic Nudge v1.1 - Discourage Contact (3,9)\"\ntags: \"nudging, systematic-nudge, basin-evasion, slsqp, sota-push\"\nabstract: \"This is the first experiment\
    \ in my 'Systematic Nudging' research arc. It takes the sparse SOTA packing from Eval 641 and applies a 'discouragement nudge' to a single key contact: (3,9). The goal is to force the optimizer out of the dominant SOTA basin by breaking its existing structure. This controlled, methodical approach is a direct test of the hypothesis that targeted structural disruption can lead to the discovery of a new, superior optimum.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n\n  BASE_CENTERS = np.array([[8.46873013e-02, 8.46873013e-02], [1.32360094e-01, 2.96434501e-01], [7.82692709e-02, 5.00000000e-01], [1.32360094e-01, 7.03565499e-01], [8.46873013e-02, 9.15312699e-01], [2.73531650e-01, 1.05276079e-01], [3.81125065e-01, 2.99112331e-01], [2.69793959e-01, 5.00000000e-01], [3.81125065e-01, 7.00887669e-01], [2.73531650e-01, 8.94723921e-01], [4.82519013e-01, 1.03717099e-01], [5.96528648e-01, 2.73192781e-01], [5.32519668e-01,\
    \ 5.00000000e-01], [5.96528648e-01, 7.26807219e-01], [4.82519013e-01, 8.96282901e-01], [6.82251639e-01, 9.61584984e-02], [7.63249164e-01, 2.40501408e-01], [7.42587601e-01, 4.04280278e-01], [7.42587601e-01, 5.95719722e-01], [6.82251639e-01, 9.03841502e-01], [8.88936708e-01, 1.11063292e-01], [9.07544188e-01, 3.13729982e-01], [9.06180804e-01, 5.00000000e-01], [9.07544188e-01, 6.86270018e-01], [8.88936708e-01, 8.88936708e-01], [7.63249164e-01, 7.59498592e-01]])\n  BASE_RADII = np.array([8.46872913e-02, 1.32360084e-01, 7.82692609e-02, 1.32360084e-01, 8.46872913e-02, 1.05276069e-01, 1.16419283e-01, 1.13255412e-01, 1.16419283e-01, 1.05276069e-01, 1.03717089e-01, 1.00538135e-01, 1.35128279e-01, 1.00538137e-01, 1.03717089e-01, 9.61584884e-02, 6.93572823e-02, 9.57197149e-02, 9.57197171e-02, 9.61584884e-02, 1.11063282e-01, 9.24558017e-02, 9.38191856e-02, 9.24558017e-02, 1.11063282e-01, 6.93572798e-02])\n\n  def _ensure_validity(c, r):\n      for i in range(N): r[i] = min(r[i], c[i,0], 1-c[i,0],\
    \ c[i,1], 1-c[i,1])\n      for _ in range(10):\n          violations = 0;\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j]); rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                  if dist < rad_sum: violations+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY); r[i]*=scale; r[j]*=scale\n          if violations == 0: break\n      return c, np.maximum(r, 0)\n  \n  def z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      contacts_to_discourage = [(3, 9)]\n      \n      def nudge_objective(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          base_obj = -np.sum(r)\n          penalty = 0\n          for i, j in contacts_to_discourage:\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n              target_dist = r[i] + r[j] + 0.01 # EPS_FAR\n              penalty += 1e1 * max(0, target_dist - dist)**2 # BETA_DISCOURAGE\n          return base_obj + penalty\n\n      bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n  \
    \    def ineq_boundary(z): c,r=z_to_cr(z); return np.concatenate([c[:,0]-r, 1-(c[:,0]+r), c[:,1]-r, 1-(c[:,1]+r)])\n      def ineq_nonoverlap(z): c,r=z_to_cr(z); diff=c[:,None,:]-c[None,:,:]; dist=np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2,axis=-1)); iu=np.triu_indices(N,1); return dist[iu]-(r[iu[0]]+r[iu[1]])\n      constraints = [{'type':'ineq','fun':ineq_boundary}, {'type':'ineq','fun':ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n      initial_z = np.concatenate([BASE_CENTERS.flatten(), BASE_RADII])\n      res = minimize(nudge_objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 2000, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n      \n      final_centers, final_radii = z_to_cr(res.x)\n      return _ensure_validity(final_centers, final_radii)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Prometheus III: Systematic Nudge v1.2 - Discourage Contact (7,12)\"\ntags: \"nudging, systematic-nudge, basin-evasion, slsqp, sota-push\"\nabstract: \"This is the second experiment in my 'Systematic Nudging' research\
    \ arc. It is identical to v1.1, but targets the other key contact of the sparse SOTA packing from Eval 641: (7,12). By systematically and independently disrupting the core structural components of a known SOTA, I aim to map the adjacent basins of the solution landscape and identify a path to a superior optimum.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n\n  BASE_CENTERS = np.array([[8.46873013e-02, 8.46873013e-02], [1.32360094e-01, 2.96434501e-01], [7.82692709e-02, 5.00000000e-01], [1.32360094e-01, 7.03565499e-01], [8.46873013e-02, 9.15312699e-01], [2.73531650e-01, 1.05276079e-01], [3.81125065e-01, 2.99112331e-01], [2.69793959e-01, 5.00000000e-01], [3.81125065e-01, 7.00887669e-01], [2.73531650e-01, 8.94723921e-01], [4.82519013e-01, 1.03717099e-01], [5.96528648e-01, 2.73192781e-01], [5.32519668e-01, 5.00000000e-01], [5.96528648e-01, 7.26807219e-01], [4.82519013e-01, 8.96282901e-01], [6.82251639e-01, 9.61584984e-02],\
    \ [7.63249164e-01, 2.40501408e-01], [7.42587601e-01, 4.04280278e-01], [7.42587601e-01, 5.95719722e-01], [6.82251639e-01, 9.03841502e-01], [8.88936708e-01, 1.11063292e-01], [9.07544188e-01, 3.13729982e-01], [9.06180804e-01, 5.00000000e-01], [9.07544188e-01, 6.86270018e-01], [8.88936708e-01, 8.88936708e-01], [7.63249164e-01, 7.59498592e-01]])\n  BASE_RADII = np.array([8.46872913e-02, 1.32360084e-01, 7.82692609e-02, 1.32360084e-01, 8.46872913e-02, 1.05276069e-01, 1.16419283e-01, 1.13255412e-01, 1.16419283e-01, 1.05276069e-01, 1.03717089e-01, 1.00538135e-01, 1.35128279e-01, 1.00538137e-01, 1.03717089e-01, 9.61584884e-02, 6.93572823e-02, 9.57197149e-02, 9.57197171e-02, 9.61584884e-02, 1.11063282e-01, 9.24558017e-02, 9.38191856e-02, 9.24558017e-02, 1.11063282e-01, 6.93572798e-02])\n\n  def _ensure_validity(c, r):\n      for i in range(N): r[i] = min(r[i], c[i,0], 1-c[i,0], c[i,1], 1-c[i,1])\n      for _ in range(10):\n          violations = 0;\n          for i in range(N):\n              for\
    \ j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j]); rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                  if dist < rad_sum: violations+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY); r[i]*=scale; r[j]*=scale\n          if violations == 0: break\n      return c, np.maximum(r, 0)\n  \n  def z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      contacts_to_discourage = [(7, 12)]\n      \n      def nudge_objective(z):\n          c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          base_obj = -np.sum(r)\n          penalty = 0\n          for i, j in contacts_to_discourage:\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n              target_dist = r[i] + r[j] + 0.01 # EPS_FAR\n              penalty += 1e1 * max(0, target_dist - dist)**2 # BETA_DISCOURAGE\n          return base_obj + penalty\n\n      bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n      def ineq_boundary(z): c,r=z_to_cr(z); return np.concatenate([c[:,0]-r, 1-(c[:,0]+r), c[:,1]-r, 1-(c[:,1]+r)])\n     \
    \ def ineq_nonoverlap(z): c,r=z_to_cr(z); diff=c[:,None,:]-c[None,:,:]; dist=np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2,axis=-1)); iu=np.triu_indices(N,1); return dist[iu]-(r[iu[0]]+r[iu[1]])\n      constraints = [{'type':'ineq','fun':ineq_boundary}, {'type':'ineq','fun':ineq_nonoverlap}]\n\n      initial_z = np.concatenate([BASE_CENTERS.flatten(), BASE_RADII])\n      res = minimize(nudge_objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 2000, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n      \n      final_centers, final_radii = z_to_cr(res.x)\n      return _ensure_validity(final_centers, final_radii)\n```"
